{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194207": {
      "title": "Head of the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering Location: Hong Kong The University invites applications and nominations for the position of Head of the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering. The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) is a world-class university known for its innovative education, research excellence, and impactful knowledge transfer. With a holistic and interdisciplinary pedagogy approach, HKUST was ranked 6th in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026, 3rd in the Times Higher Education’s Young University Rankings 2026, and 20th globally and 1st in Hong Kong in the Times Higher Education’s Impact Rankings 2026. Eleven HKUST subjects were ranked among the world’s top 50 in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026, with “Civil and Structural Engineering” coming in 27th worldwide. Our graduates are highly competitive, consistently ranking among the world’s top 30 most sought-after employees. As of January 2026, HKUST members have founded over 1,900 active start-ups, including 10 Unicorns and 21 exits (IPO or M&A). The Department The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CIVL) at HKUST invites applications from outstanding candidates with the vision, energy, and leadership potential to help shape the next stage of the Department’s development. CIVL comprises more than 35 faculty members and serves approximately 480 undergraduate students and 300 postgraduate research students. The Department offers BEng, MSc, MPhil, and PhD programs. The Department conducts comprehensive teaching and research across fundamental and applied areas of civil and environmental engineering. Building on HKUST’s strengths in science, engineering, innovation, and interdisciplinary collaborations, CIVL seeks to tackle pressing global and regional challenges in building smart, resilient, sustainable, healthy and inclusive communities. Its expertise spans infrastructure resilience, climate adaptation, sustainable urban systems, environmental protection, water resources, geotechnical and structural engineering, transportation, autonomous construction technology, and the digital transformation of built environment. The Department is supported by a wide range of research platforms, advanced laboratories, and experimental, computational, and field research capabilities, featuring a State Key Laboratory and a Chinese National Engineering Research Center, and having launched the Hong Kong’s first satellite. CIVL has established strengths in sensing, monitoring, data analytics, and digital and space technologies for civil and environmental engineering applications. The Department also benefits from partnerships with industry, and has a strong record of competitive funding, professional engagement, and societal impact. We seek candidates who can bring a bold, forward-looking, and inclusive academic vision; strengthen existing areas of excellence; open new interdisciplinary directions; and contribute to CIVL’s continued development in research, education, knowledge transfer, and global engagement. The successful candidate is expected to help enhance the Department’s academic reputation, attract and mentor outstanding students and faculty, foster collaboration across disciplines, and advance CIVL’s standing as a world-leading, innovative department in Hong Kong, the Greater Bay Area, and beyond. The Role & Terms Reporting to the Dean of Engineering, the Head of CIVL is expected to provide leadership for the Department and manage its diverse academic and administrative functions. Concurrent with a tenured professorial appointment, the Head appointment will typically be for an initial 3-year term and may be renewable for a second term. Competitive remuneration and generous fringe benefits, including housing where appropriate, will be provided. Applications/nominations for the position are invited from well-qualified and accomplished scholars.  In addition to extensive teaching and research experience, the successful candidate must have demonstrated capability to provide strong leadership in academic administration at tertiary level.  Proven capacity to interact effectively with government, industry and commercial sectors is an advantage. Applications/nominations, together with full curriculum vitae and names and email addresses of three referees, should be sent through the HKUST recruitment system. Review of candidates will start immediately and the search will continue until the position is filled. For more information about the University, the School of Engineering and the CIVL Department, please visit http://www.hkust.edu.hk/ , https://seng.hkust.edu.hk/ , and https://ce.hkust.edu.hk respectively."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193481": {
      "title": "Head of Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering Location: Hong Kong The University invites applications and nominations for the position of Head of the Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering. The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) is a world-class university known for its innovative education, research excellence, and impactful knowledge transfer. With a holistic and interdisciplinary pedagogy approach, HKUST was ranked 6th in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026, 3rd in the Times Higher Education’s Young University Rankings 2026, and 20th globally and 1st in Hong Kong in the Times Higher Education’s Impact Rankings 2026. Eleven HKUST subjects were ranked among the world’s top 50 in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026, with “Electrical and Electronic Engineering” coming in 33th worldwide and first in Hong Kong. Our graduates are highly competitive, consistently ranking among the world’s top 30 most sought-after employees. As of January 2026, HKUST members have founded over 1,900 active start-ups, including 10 Unicorns and 21 exits (IPO or M&A). The Department The Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering ( ECE) currently has 44 tenured-track faculty members, out of which 17 are IEEE Fellows, and 11 are Fellows of other renowned professional organizations (including a member of the National Academy of Engineering USA).  Offering academic degrees in BEng, MPhil, MSc, and PhD, to about 770 undergraduate students and over 550 postgraduate research students, the Department has a broad and distinguished coverage in Integrated Circuits and Systems, Wireless Communications and Networks, Control and Robotic Systems, Biomedical Engineering, Microelectronics, Photonics, Quantum Engineering, and Data Science and AI. We are at the forefronts of AI chips, 6G wireless technology, robotics, drones and automated vehicles. Our faculty work on electronic engineering innovations that enable an integrative perspective of both software and hardware. We combine system level integrated solutions that can address societal needs. Our faculty hold major collaborative research programs including two Area of Excellence (AoE) in 6G wireless communications and in Aging and Health, Strategic research topics in wide-bandgap and ultra-wide-bandgap semiconductor microelectronics, collaborative research fund in brain machine interfaces and neuro diseases, and research impact fund in AI-assisted image analysis for diseases diagnostics. The Role & Terms Reporting to the Dean of Engineering, the Head of ECE is expected to provide leadership for the Department and manage its diverse academic and administrative functions. Concurrent with a tenured professorial appointment, the Head appointment will typically be for an initial 3-year term and may be renewable for a second term. Competitive remuneration and generous fringe benefits, including housing where appropriate, will be provided. Applications and nominations are invited from well-qualified and accomplished scholars.  The successful candidate must have extensive teaching and research experience, a broad knowledge base, and an open mindset to inclusively appreciate the full scope of ECE areas. They should be a visionary leader with strong academic administration skills at the tertiary level, managing decisions and resource allocation with fairness and impartiality. As an excellent communicator, the candidate will facilitate growth across all areas of the department and be willing to dedicate ample time to actively support and guide it to achieve meaningful impact. Additionally, proven capacity to collaborate effectively with government, industry and commercial sectors is an advantage. Applications/nominations, together with full curriculum vitae and names and email addresses of three referees, should be sent through the HKUST recruitment system.  Review of candidates will start from 15 November 2026 and the search will continue until the position is filled. For more information about the University, the School of Engineering and the ECE Department, please visit http://www.hkust.edu.hk/ , https://seng.hkust.edu.hk/ , and https://ece.hkust.edu.hk/ respectively."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192787": {
      "title": "Teaching-Track Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies Location: Hong Kong The Dual Degree Program (DDP) in Technology & Management at HKUST is a prestigious and innovative program designed to cultivate leaders who excel in both technology and business management. We are seeking a dynamic and innovative teaching-track faculty member to design and implement a comprehensive undergraduate curriculum, and teach at the undergraduate level. The ideal candidate should possess a strong background in both technology and business management, and substantial real-world experience. This role requires a passion for teaching and a commitment to fostering tomorrow's leaders through a cutting-edge educational experience. Find more in: https://techmgmt.hkust.edu.hk/ Applicants should possess at least a Master's degree in technology, engineering, business management, entrepreneurship, innovation, or related disciplines. A PhD in a technology or engineering discipline is desirable; or an MBA will be an advantage Work experience in computer science, information technology, artificial intelligence, engineering, management consulting, startup or related disciplines preferred Professional experience in consulting, preferably with a reputable consulting firm with strong understanding of problem-solving and case analysis methodology, consulting practices, and contemporary business strategies Proven experience in curriculum development and instructional design, preferably at the undergraduate level Demonstrated ability to teach and mentor students in management consulting, innovation, entrepreneurship, problem-solving, technology commercialization, and related methodologies Proficiency in integrating technology and experiential learning approaches into educational settings Excellent communication, collaboration, and interpersonal skills Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits. Housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of the contract. Please submit the following documents for the application: Curriculum Vitae Teaching statement Past teaching record and evaluation (if applicable) Name and contact Information for three qualified referees The applicants must first sign up or create a personal account.  Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and candidates are strongly encouraged to submit applications as soon as possible and applications will be considered until the openings are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192419": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas Location: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas The Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas (EMIA) is an academic unit established under the Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies. EMIA envisions to foster the agile development of new education programs; contribute to identifying emerging cutting edge and niche topics, such as Artificial Intelligence, Digital Media and Creative Arts; and coordinate interdisciplinary education and research initiatives within and outside HKUST for agile development of emerging areas.  EMIA will serve as a cross-disciplinary platform facilitating scholars from different departments, campuses, and universities to incubate and drive research agenda for new and emerging interdisciplinary areas. Successful applicants will be expected to participate in or lead collaborative teams and research on emerging interdisciplinary topics, nurture undergraduate and postgraduate students with an interdisciplinary approach, and drive various interdisciplinary initiatives of the Division. Senior Tenure Track/Tenured Position in DDP One of the positions is at the Associate or Full Professor level and is affiliated with the Dual Degree Program (DDP) in Technology & Management, a prestigious and innovative program designed to cultivate leaders who excel in both technology and business management, under the Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies. Applicants for this senior position must hold a PhD in Engineering or Technology, and possess substantial management experience in the technology sector or a proven track record of teaching technology management. The successful applicant is expected to assume a leadership role within DDP. Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Fringe benefits, including annual leave, medical and dental benefits, and housing benefits, will be provided where applicable. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of the contract. Applications should be submitted via Interfolio together with (i) a full CV, (ii) research statement and teaching philosophy, (iii) five representative research papers, (iv) a letter of interest summarizing your qualifications, areas of expertise and career goals, and (v) name and contact information of at least three referees. Review of applications will start from 24 September 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192777": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Location: Hong Kong The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology is a world-renowned, international research university in Hong Kong, ranked among the top universities in Asia. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty and has a range of family-friendly policies in place. The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering https://mae.hkust.edu.hk// (MAE) has comprehensive teaching, and basic and applied research programs. There are currently 30+ faculty members, about 450 undergraduate students and 450 postgraduate students in the department. Our research activities are well supported by multi-disciplinary research facilities and collaborations across the university. The MAE Department invites applications for multiple faculty positions at all ranks (Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor). We welcome outstanding candidates in all research areas of the department, including but not limited to robotics, aerospace, advanced materials, green and smart manufacturing, and sustainable energy systems. Applicants must have a PhD degree in mechanical engineering or a related field, a strong record of scholarly publications, and recognized research and/or industrial experience. Successful candidates are expected to establish an externally funded research program and contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching. Appointment at all ranks (Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor) will be considered. Competitive salaries commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Ample opportunities for professional growth and development are available.  Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits, annual leave and housing benefits, where applicable, will be provided. Appointment as Professor will be on substantive basis while appointment as Assistant / Associate Professor will normally be on a three-year contract. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. To apply, please include the following documents in PDF format: 1) Curriculum Vitae with a full publication list; 2) Statement of Contribution detailing 3-5 leading published works; 3) Teaching Statement; 4) Research Statement; 5) Names and Contact Information of at least three referees; and 6) Research Areas of Interest (Robotics, Aerospace, Advanced Materials, Green and Smart Manufacturing, Sustainable Energy Systems) All applications materials should be submitted via Interfolio which is accessible from the HKUST Recruitment Portal ( https://hkustcareers.hkust.edu.hk/join-us/current-opening/academic-careers ). Interested applicants may click the [ Apply Now ] button on the position page; or directly to https://apply.interfolio.com/192777 . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue on a rolling basis. For full consideration, applications should be received by December 18, 2026 ; however, positions will remain open until filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192666": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Lecturer I / Lecturer II (several posts)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Medicine Location: Hong Kong The School of Medicine invites applications for full-time Teaching-Track Faculty positions (Senior Lecturer / Lecturer I / Lecturer II) in the following expertise fields (several posts), expected to begin in Fall 2027. Biochemistry Pharmacology Physiology Anatomy Microbiology Bioengineering The appointee is expected to teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses offered by the School of Medicine. Duties include, but not limited to, teaching lectures, conducting tutorials and demonstrations, supporting curriculum design, and developing teaching materials.  The appointee will also participate in course and curriculum development, advise and mentor students, support project-based and experiential learning activities, and provide student-related services.  The appointee will work closely with a team of colleagues dedicated to the development and delivery of innovative pedagogical approaches to improve student learning, and perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of Medicine or the delegates. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in the relevant discipline, or a closely-related medical discipline, and be able to teach in English. They should possess solid teaching and student mentoring experience in tertiary education (minimum 2-4 years for Lecturer II; 4-6 years for Lecturer I; 6-8 years for Senior Lecturer), as well as excellent communication and organizational skills.  Experience in teaching interdisciplinary core curriculum courses will be an advantage. Terms An initial contract will be for two years and is renewable subject to performance review and mutual agreement.  Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided.  A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Applications including 1) a cover letter, 2) a full curriculum vitae, 3) names and contact information of at least three referees, and 4) a teaching statement (all in PDF format) should be submitted via Interfolio which is accessible from the HKUST Recruitment Portal ( https://hkustcareers.hkust.edu.hk/join-us/current-opening/academic-careers ). Interested applicants may click the [Apply Now] button on the position page; or directly to https://apply.interfolio.com/192666 .  Applications are accepted at any time and considered on a rolling basis.  Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. Applicants will receive an acknowledgement by email upon successful submission. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192663": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Operations Management",
      "description": "Posted: Sep 01, 2026 Deadline: Oct 16, 2026 Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management - OM group Location: Hong Kong T en ure-track Faculty Positions in Operations Management The Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics, and Operations Management (ISOM) at the School of Business and Management, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST), is seeking applicants for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level in Operations Management, expected to begin in July 2027. The Operations Management group within the department offers undergraduate, MSc, and PhD programs, as well as courses for the school’s MBA, EMBA, DBA, and Executive Education programs. The group plays a major role in the HKUST Li & Fung Supply Chain Institute. The department's website is http://www.bm.ust.hk/~isom . Candidates should hold a PhD degree (or be near completion) in Operations Management or closely related disciplines and have a strong record (or demonstrate strong competence for the Assistant Professor rank) in both research and teaching. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), teaching evaluations (if any), and two selected research papers, and arrange for three reference letters to be submitted by the writers. All materials should be submitted via Interfolio by October 16, 2026. For candidates presenting at the INFORMS 2026 conference, please also provide the titles, times, and venues of the presentations."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191029": {
      "title": "2027 All Fields in Economics (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Economics Location: Hong Kong The HKUST Department of Economics is seeking to fill multiple positions in all fields of economics at any rank (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor). We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in Applied Microeconomics (Labor, Health, Development etc.). Outstanding candidates in other areas are also encouraged to apply. Salary is highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The university offers a comprehensive fringe benefit package, including medical/dental care, annual leave, and housing benefits, for eligible appointees. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a contract for appointment on contract terms. Teaching may be at the undergraduate, MSc. and Ph.D. levels. HKUST is a world-renowned English-speaking international research university in Asia's most vibrant city. The Department of Economics at HKUST strives to excel in both its research and teaching missions. In 2025, the Economics Department was ranked No. 27 in the world, No. 4 in Asia, and No. 1 in Hong Kong, according to the QS World University Rankings by Subject—Economics & Econometrics. Please visit our websites at https://econ.hkust.edu.hk/homepage for more detailed information. Candidates must receive a Ph.D. by August 2027 and must demonstrate the potential to achieve excellence in both research and teaching at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Applicants must include curriculum vitae, recent publications or research papers. Please submit your application electronically through the link Apply Now at the end of this page. Junior and mid-career applicants should arrange for 3 letters of recommendation to be sent. For tenured positions, references will be solicited only after both sides agree to proceed with the process of appointment. Review of applications begins immediately and will be accepted until the position is filled. Shortlisted junior and mid-career candidates will be interviewed via Zoom in late December 2026 or early January 2027. For full consideration, junior and mid-career applications, including a curriculum vitae, recent publications, research papers, and three letters of recommendation, must be submitted electronically by November 22, 2026, at 11:59 PM Eastern Time. Inquiries can be addressed to econjob@ust.hk"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191104": {
      "title": "Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Computer Science and Engineering Location: Hong Kong The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology The Department of Computer Science and Engineering ( https://cse.hkust.edu.hk/ ) at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) invites applications for substantiation-track faculty positions at the ranks of Professor, Associate Professor and Assistant Professor for the 2027-2028 academic year. We are looking for outstanding candidates in all areas of computer science and engineering who can complement or add to our existing strengths in the areas of Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, Database, Human-Computer Interaction, Networking and Computer Systems, Software Engineering and Programming Languages, Theoretical Computer Science, and Vision and Graphics. As a champion of diversity, we welcome female and international candidates. The Department has over 50 regular faculty members, recruited from major universities and research institutions around the world, and more than 2,300 students (including about 930 postgraduate students). HKUST is ranked among the best young universities in the world, and is committed to increasing the gender and ethnic diversity of its faculty with a range of family-friendly policies in place. The medium of instruction is English. All candidates must have a PhD degree in Computer Science or related fields by the time of appointment. Salary and startup package are highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include medical/dental benefits and annual leave. Housing will also be provided where applicable. Assistant Professor appointments will initially be on a three-year contract. A gratuity will be payable upon completion of contract. Applications including 1) a cover letter, 2) a full curriculum vitae, 3) names and contact information of at least three referees, 4) a research statement, and 5) a teaching statement (all in PDF format) should be submitted via Interfolio which is accessible from the HKUST Recruitment Portal ( https://hkustcareers.hkust.edu.hk/join-us/current-opening/academic-careers ). Interested applicants may click the [ Apply Now ] button on the position page; or directly to https://dossier.interfolio.com/apply/191104 . Priority will be given to applications received by Thursday, 31 December 2026 . Please be advised that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191744": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Faculty Positions (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Materials Location: Hong Kong Open-Rank Faculty Positions (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) Department of Materials School of Engineering The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology The Department of Materials at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) invites applications for substantiation-track faculty positions at all ranks, including Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Professor. We seek outstanding scholars whose research advances the multidisciplinary frontiers of materials science, engineering, and intelligence. Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to: Materials for health and biomedicine Materials for energy and information Engineering materials for terrestrial and space sustainability Advanced materials modeling and characterization AI-empowered and autonomous materials synthesis and discovery The Department aspires to become an impact-driven, interdisciplinary hub for materials innovation, advancing the discovery, development, and translation of cutting-edge materials technologies in health, energy, information, and sustainability while addressing pressing global challenges and strategic national priorities. Successful candidates are expected to contribute to the Department’s mission by: Educating and nurturing future leaders through rigorous, interdisciplinary teaching, mentoring, and research experiences that provide students with a strong foundation in materials science, engineering, and intelligence. Conducting cutting-edge and transformative research that addresses major scientific, technological, and societal challenges in areas such as biomedical and health technologies, energy and information, advanced manufacturing, and sustainability. Advancing innovation and entrepreneurship by translating fundamental discoveries into technologies and commercial applications, mentoring students and researchers in innovation, and contributing to economic development, societal well-being, and strategic technological advancement. Fostering interdisciplinary collaboration across materials science, engineering, artificial intelligence, data science, and related disciplines within HKUST and with academic, industrial, and governmental partners. The Department will offer a comprehensive portfolio of academic programs at the BSc, MSc, MPhil, and PhD levels, providing faculty members with opportunities to develop innovative curricula, establish world-class research programs, and mentor the next generation of materials scientists and engineers. We welcome applications from suitable candidates who share our ambition to redefine the future of materials research. Applicants should hold a PhD in materials science and engineering, physics, chemistry, or a closely related engineering field. Successful candidates are expected to develop strong, independent, and innovative externally funded research programs; teach effectively in MSEI and related courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and actively participate in service to the Department, School, and University. Interested candidates are invited to upload a full curriculum vitae, statements of research and teaching, and the names of three referees, along with their email addresses and affiliations. For enquiries, please send them to dmat@ust.hk . Review of applications will start immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191647": {
      "title": "Teaching Track Faculty Position",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Computer Science and Engineering Location: Hong Kong The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology Department of Computer Science and Engineering The Department of Computer Science and Engineering at HKUST is one of the best in the world, with a vision to be the leading global research, education and innovation hub in Computer Science and AI. Our areas of impact include AI and Machine Learning, Data Science, and Computer Systems. Our department includes highly awarded and cited faculty, including many ACM and IEEE Fellows. Learn more about the Department of Computer Science and Engineering at https://cse.hkust.edu.hk/ The Department invites applications for a full-time teaching-track faculty position on Lecturer or Senior Lecturer rank in the area of computer science and artificial intelligence on renewable contract terms commencing February 2027. About the Role The appointee will play an important role in the development and teaching of computer science courses for MSc programs.  They are responsible for developing and teaching MSc courses in some of the MSc programs under the Department, including MSc(AIE), MSc(AI), MSc(IT) and MSc(BDT), with working locations in both Hong Kong (HKUST Clear Water Bay campus and its associate teaching facilities) and Shanghai (HKUST Shanghai Centre). They will be required to travel regularly between Hong Kong and Shanghai for one of the MSc programs, MSc AIE. The appointee is required to teach some of the MSc courses related to “Advanced Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship” and courses relevant to computer science, big data and artificial intelligence, and is expected to: coordinate seminars, workshops, student presentations, etc.; and mentor students in internship and entrepreneurship initiatives with Shanghai as the main work location arrange student activities and handle inquiries related to the MSc AIE program perform duties as assigned by the MSc AIE program (Optional) design and teach a course in Advanced Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship with Hong Kong as the main work location Required Qualifications A PhD degree in computer science from a reputable university Strong technical knowledge and skills in one or more relevant areas (e.g., AI/ML algorithms, data analytics, application of AI, IT and big data technologies) Prior experience with entrepreneurship (e.g., having participated in startup projects, product commercialization and/or venture competitions) Preferred/Bonus Qualifications Demonstrated capacity for excellent teaching at tertiary level or elsewhere Experience in service-related matters (e.g., interviewing student applicants; academic counselling; and organizing seminars, industrial visits, career fairs and other activities for students) Passion for supporting young innovators and helping students translate conceptual ideas into practical solutions (Duration: 1 year, renewable) Candidates with outstanding performance may be considered for a 2-year contract and/or the title of Assistant to Associate Professor of Engineering Education at the time of contract renewal. The Department is a leading intellectual center for computer science research with a group of committed faculty members with demonstrated excellence in scholarship and teaching. HKUST provides a supportive teaching environment, strong teaching support staff and leading-edge facilities. Courses are conducted in English. Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only. Applications including 1) a cover letter, 2) a full curriculum vitae, 3) names and contact information of at least three referees, and 4) a teaching statement (all in PDF format) should be submitted via Interfolio which is accessible from the HKUST Recruitment Portal ( https://hkustcareers.hkust.edu.hk/join-us/current-opening/academic-careers ). Interested applicants may click the [Apply Now] button on the position page; or directly to https://apply.interfolio.com/191647 .  Priority will be given to applications received by Tuesday, 1 September 2026. Please be advised that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190076": {
      "title": "Faculty Position(s) in Biodiversity, Ecosystem Services, and Nature-based Solutions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Environment and Sustainability Location: Hong Kong The Division of Environment and Sustainability at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology is seeking applicants for substantiation-track faculty positions at all ranks (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor) in the field of Biodiversity, Ecosystem Services, and Nature-based Solutions . We invite candidates whose scholarly interests intersect with multiple areas of sustainability and sustainable development. The successful candidates will play a crucial role in advancing the University’s sustainability education strategy by providing leadership, energy, and vision to a well-balanced and multi-disciplinary approach to understanding key concepts, principles, theories, and practices related to biodiversity and ecosystem services. Candidates are expected to develop or contribute to an internationally recognized research program that emphasizes collaborative research aimed at addressing complex global challenges, including biodiversity loss, ecosystem degradation, climate change impacts, and the sustainable management of natural resources/nature-based solutions. Candidates should have a strong understanding of experiential “hands-on” learning as a means of instruction for students, and an exemplary teaching record.  Successful applicants will be expected to participate in or lead collaborative interdisciplinary research teams focused on biodiversity conservation, ecosystem services assessment, and the integration of ecological models into decision-making processes under the Division’s three research themes: Air and Health Climate Adaptation and Resilience (CARE) Sustainable Finance and Net Zero Solutions The Division of Environment and Sustainability is an interdisciplinary academic unit dedicated to the use and management of natural resources in an economically efficient, environmentally compatible, and socially responsible manner.  Our faculty members publish broadly in both disciplinary journals and diverse, environmentally focused outlets, and are rewarded for working on interdisciplinary teams in applied contexts.  Depending on the candidate’s areas of expertise, a joint appointment between the Division of Environment and Sustainability and a relevant academic Department/Division may be possible. A doctoral degree in ecology, environmental science, biology, or a related interdisciplinary field with a focus on biodiversity, ecosystem services or nature-based solutions. Proven teaching and advising experience at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. A strong research and publication record consistent with the candidate’s academic rank, along with evidence of potential for securing research funding. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in interdisciplinary teams, engaging both social and natural scientists. Interested candidates should complete the online application via Interfolio by clicking the \"Apply Now\" button on this page.  Please include the following application materials through Interfolio: A cover letter summarizing qualifications, areas of expertise, and career goals Full curriculum vitae Research Statement Teaching Statement Contact Information for three qualified referees Review of applications will start in early August 2026 and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189742": {
      "title": "Director of the Center for Language Education",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Humanities and Social Science Location: Center for Language Education, HKUST, Clear Water Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong SAR Job Functions The Director provides leadership and vision to achieve excellence in language education at HKUST. With responsibility for a Center at the cutting edge, this role offers a great opportunity to shape the future of language education particularly in Human-AI interaction for language learning at scale. Reporting to the Dean of the School of Humanities and Social Science, a strong applicant will: be a leader in language education research with an international profile, providing a visible external face which brings recognition to current innovation in language education, while also building on strengths of the Center for positive impact in the language education sector; provide strategic leadership and vision for CLE, and the Center’s goals and initiatives for language teaching, learning and assessment; maximise technological innovation for teaching in a way that strictly adheres to pedagogic principles and ethical use; ensure teaching of the highest standard of quality assurance which challenges all students to work to their potential; work collaboratively with departments and units in the University to ensure an approach to language education that aligns with university practices and priorities; be transparent in decision-making, with effective communication within and beyond the CLE; effectively deploy human, financial, and other resources. Additionally, the CLE Director also holds the title of Associate Dean, working closely with the Associate Provost Teaching & Learning to ensure delivery of the mission of the University with regard to language education. The CLE Director may hold a concurrent appointment as Associate Professor/Professor as appropriate depending on the qualifications of the candidate. Terms & Applications/Nominations Terms of appointment and remuneration are highly competitive. Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including housing, annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided as applicable to contract type. Fixed term contract holders will receive gratuity payable upon completion of the contract. Appointment to the position will be offered a three-year fixed-term contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. If appropriate, research active applicants with a substantial publication record may be considered for a substantiation track appointment. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in an area relevant to language education; a distinguished record of academic research/scholarship in the areas of AI in language studies, applied linguistics or language learning, or related disciplines; demonstrated commitment to excellence and leadership in curriculum development and pedagogy; a track record of driving innovation in AI and language education with an understanding of the place of language education in a prestigious EMI university in Hong Kong; substantial experience leveraging digital technologies for language teaching and learning, with a depth of understanding of the potential for AI in communication that is both effective and ethical; administrative capability to lead a large academic teaching unit, including resource management and team-building abilities; excellent communication skills for use in a multilingual and multicultural academic environment, and with stakeholders external to the CLE, both within the university and beyond. Center for Language Education The Center for Language Education (CLE) is an academic teaching unit within the School of Humanities and Social Science (SHSS). The primary mission of the CLE is to deliver the University’s UGC-funded language enhancement programs for English and Chinese to UG and PG students from all Schools in the University.  The CLE has 66 full-time teaching staff (16 Senior Lecturers, 44 Lecturer I, and 6 Lecturer II), 9 teaching/project support staff and 16 non-academic support staff including its own full-time Instructional Designer. The CLE has a dynamic and progressive outlook with a mindset of continuous adaptation to meet evolving needs. In 2024-26, it delivered a fully revamped English and Chinese curriculum: a new English curriculum with two pathways and a new Chinese curriculum with two streams: i) Chinese as a Foreign Language for non-Chinese background students and ii) Chinese for Specific Purposes for students with Chinese proficiency from HKDSE Level 3 through to native Mandarin speakers. The CLE’s newly introduced curriculum also offers a rich set of elective choices including Communication courses and elective Broadening courses within the University’s Common Core. Additionally, the Center makes a strong contribution to a Master of Arts degree in International Language Education with separate concentrations in English and Chinese teaching. It runs a small but growing third-languages program, including Japanese, Spanish, French and Korean and an active program of experiential engagement activities to promote language and AI, and culture. The Center also has a strong scholarly orientation including securing teaching and learning grants. Together with the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, it recently secured HKD 30 million in QEF funding to develop an AI-assisted VR English speaking programme for secondary schools. The Center has a robust, internal management structure and enjoys strong support from the University senior management. This has made it a leader among language centers especially in pedagogical innovation — combining AI and other technologies with a humanistic commitment to the learner, grounded in the latest scholarship and research in language education. A particular strength is its Human-AI orchestration approach, positioning educators and students not as users of AI but as active orchestrators of it, keeping human judgment and connection at its centre. HKUST Founded in 1991, HKUST is a publicly funded international university dedicated to undergraduate and postgraduate education and research in science, engineering, business & management, and humanities & social science. We seek to nurture students with entrepreneurial spirit, innovative thinking, and global outlook and strive to work together to make a strong societal impact. The University is ranked as one of the most international universities in Asia comprising four Schools and an Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies and multiple research institutes/central research facilities; and the Hong Kong government has recently endorsed our competitive bid to develop a new Medical School. While actively growing, at present there are around 970 faculty members, and an enrollment of about 11,000 undergraduate and 8,700 postgraduate students. English is the language used in all teaching, research, and administration. HKUST is celebrating its 35th Anniversary this year with a strong presence in global higher education. It has received many international recognitions including citations and rankings; for example, HKUST ranks 6th in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026 , 3rd in the Times Higher Education Young University Rankings 2024 , and 19th globally (1st in Hong Kong) in the Times Higher Education Impact Rankings 2025 . A total of 11 subjects offered by HKUST are ranked among the world’s top 50 in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026 . Moreover, it has consistently been ranked within the world’s top 30 in the Global Employability University Ranking, reflecting the strong competitiveness of its graduates. At the heart of the University’s pursuit of excellence in teaching, research, and societal impact lies uncompromising efforts to recruit and retain the best talents globally and locally. We seek to diversify HKUST’s critical mass of world-class academics, researchers, staff and students in order to drive cutting-edge education and research initiatives and deliver academic and administrative excellence. The University promotes a diverse learning environment that enhances student development of their creativity, innovative thinking and global outlook, especially in today’s rapidly changing society, and technological and AI development. Proactive faculty recruitment is undertaken from around the world in all disciplines of the University. HKUST upholds the values of diversity and an inclusive and collaborative community. Additional information about the University and the Center for Language Education is available on the websites https://hkust.edu.hk/ and https://cle.hkust.edu.hk/ respectively. Applications should be submitted to the School of Humanities and Social Science via Interfolio with (i) a cover letter and (ii) a full CV. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189563": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Information Systems (2 positions)",
      "description": "Posted: Jul 15, 2026 Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management - IS group Location: Hong Kong The Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management (ISOM) at the HKUST Business School invites applications for two tenure-track assistant professor/associate professor positions in the Information Systems area beginning in July 2027. Established in 1991, the HKUST Business School is ranked among the Top Business Schools in the world in terms of research, educational programs, and student and graduate quality. The IS group (with 18 tenure-track faculty) is ranked #20 for publications in ISR and MISQ (2021-2025), while HKUST Business School is ranked #27 in the UT Dallas Journals Ranking (2021-2025). Our MBA programs have been consistently ranked among the top in the world. Ranked 4th in Global Executive MBA program for 2025 (Joint program with Kellogg of Northwestern University; Financial Times) Ranked 24th in Global MBA programs for 2026 (Financial Times) Asia's No 1 by Bloomberg Businessweek (2024-2025) For further information on HKUST Business School, please visit https://bm.hkust.edu.hk/ Candidates must have received a doctorate in Information Systems or a related area by May 2027. The candidates must also have a strong commitment to high-quality research and excellent teaching. The successful candidate should have the ability to teach at both the MBA and undergraduate levels. Candidates preferably will be able to do both research and teach courses in the following areas: Cybersecurity  [Note: We are offering a new MSc in Information and Cybersecurity Management] AI, ML, Fintech  [Note: We are in the process of creating a joint HKUST-Tsinghua Research Center for the AI Economy] Health IT  [Note: HKUST is setting up a medical school] Applicants should apply online via Interfolio with CV and supporting documents (e.g. teaching and research statement, 3 reference letters, etc.). Applications will be considered till positions are filled. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interview. Interviews will be conducted on a rolling basis. For enquiry, please contact infosys@ust.hk"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189496": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Accounting Location: Dept of Accounting, Rm 6018, 6/F, Lee Shau Kee Business Bldg, Clearwater Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong. Faculty Positions Available from Fall 2027 The Department of Accounting at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seeks candidates for tenure-track faculty positions at all ranks. Visiting appointments will be considered if the tenure-track positions are not filled. ABOUT HKUST: HKUST offers a world-class faculty, state-of-the-art facilities, and a strong commitment to high-quality academic research. Reasonable teaching loads, active research workshops, generous research funding, and an extensive collection of accounting databases combine to create an excellent research environment. In recent years, HKUST has ranked among the top in the world in faculty research studies published in top academic accounting journals. The HKUST Research Symposium attracts the world's prominent scholars to exchange cutting-edge research ideas. Together with HKUST’s top-quality departments in economics, finance, information systems, management, and marketing, the HKUST Department of Accounting offers or participates in a full range of degree and executive programs. These include undergraduate, PhD, MBA, Executive MBA, MSc, and DBA programs plus a range of company and open-enrollment executive programs. HKUST's Executive MBA program offered jointly with the Kellogg School of Management at Northwestern University ranks among the top in the world, and HKUST's MBA program consistently ranks among the world's top 25 (Financial Times). HKUST was the first accounting program outside North America to be accredited by AACSB. HKUST attracts top undergraduate and graduate students from Hong Kong, Chinese mainland, and around the world. ABOUT THE CAMPUS: The spectacular 150-acre campus overlooking the South China Sea offers tranquil surroundings, lush open spaces, breathtaking views, and outstanding athletic and academic facilities just minutes from the exciting hustle and bustle of downtown Hong Kong. For more information, please visit our website at http://www.bm.ust.hk/~acct/ JOB QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates should possess a doctoral degree or be near completion of the degree and should have a serious commitment to scholarly research and teaching. Candidates should provide evidence of their ability and achievements commensurate with the rank sought. Salary, teaching load, and faculty support are comparable to top US business schools and based on qualifications. HOUSING: Housing benefits will be provided. BENEFITS: Appointments come with a 15 percent contract-end gratuity.  Health insurance and moving allowances are also provided. The maximum tax rate in Hong Kong is 15%. APPLICATION PROCEDURE: In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  Interested candidates should complete the online applcation via Interfolio by clicking the \"Apply Now\" button on this page.  Please include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a job market paper, and the contact emails of the three referees. If you have further queries, please send email to Professor Tai Yuan Chen at acctfasearch@ust.hk ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189501": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Department of Ocean Science Location: Hong Kong The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST), a world-class research institution, invites applications for tenure-track positions at all ranks within the Department of Ocean Science. We welcome outstanding candidates in all disciplines of ocean science and technology, and particularly encourage applications at the Associate Professor to Full Professor levels with research expertise in: ocean biogeochemical modeling; ocean-atmosphere interactions; cryosphere dynamics; climate variability and change; ocean remote sensing and technology; AI and data-driven oceanography; biological oceanography with a focus on higher trophic organisms; blue economy inclusive of fishery sciences. About Department of Ocean Science The Department of Ocean Science (OCES), established in 2018, is the only ocean-focused department among local universities in Hong Kong, and is committed to multidisciplinary research and education in ocean science and technology. Located in the Clear Water Bay, HKUST offers a distinctive advantage as the only university in Hong Kong with an on-campus waterfront Ocean Research Facility (OCRF)—an exceptional platform enabling innovative ocean and environmental research. We pursue studies spanning from fundamental sciences to cutting-edge technologies, while actively connecting scientific knowledge with real-world impacts through collaborations with governmental and industrial partners. We play a leading role in ocean science at the local, regional, and international levels. Applicants must hold a PhD degree in ocean science or a closely related discipline. For Assistant Professor positions, at least 2 years of post-doctoral experience is preferred.  Successful candidates should demonstrate strong research records, the potential to establish strong research programs, and a commitment to excellence in teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. The medium of instruction is English at HKUST. Appointment Terms Initial appointment is typically on a three-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. Eligible candidates at the rank of Associate Professor or above may be granted substantiated (tenured) appointments at HKUST, subject to a positive outcome through the University’s formal academic review and approval processes. A gratuity is payable upon successful completion of the contract. HKUST offers an internationally competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits; housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. The University is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty and has a range of family-friendly policies in place. Application materials including a cover letter, detailed curriculum vitae, research accomplishment and proposal (maximum 3 pages), three representative publications (for Assistant Professor level) / five representative publications (for Associate Professor level and above) , teaching statement (maximum 1 page), and at least 3 letters from referees, should be submitted as part of the application through Interfolio.  The recruitment process will continue until all positions are filled. Applicants should submit their application via HKUST recruitment website and by clicking the “Apply Now”: https://apply.interfolio.com/189501 Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application. HKUST is a world-class research institution with over 700 faculty members whose research ranges from science and engineering to business and social sciences.  Located in the Clear Water Bay area, HKUST’s campus has a magnificent ocean view and immediate access to a wide range of marine habitats for research and teaching."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187686": {
      "title": "Teaching-Track Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Arts and Machine Creativity Location: Hong Kong The Division of Arts and Machine Creativity (AMC) envisions being a leading cross-disciplinary center where technology, art, and humanities converge to foster innovative and impactful environments, talents, and works that shape the future world. Applicants should have a master’s or PhD degree in a related field and at least two years of teaching experience. Appointees are expected to develop and teach art-related courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. We value applicants who can demonstrate their enthusiasm and passion in education and promotion of Machine-assisted Art Practice (visual, sound, performing, installation, cinematic arts, etc.), Critical Studies on Arts and Machine Creativity (art history, media theory, philosophy of technology, etc.), and/or Art Management (managerial, legal, and business topics related to AI arts, NFT, etc.). Preferences will be given to candidates with teaching and/or research experience in fusing new technologies (e.g., generative AI) with arts. Candidates with less experience will be considered as Lecturer I. Depending on the candidate’s areas of expertise, a joint appointment between the AMC and a relevant academic Department/Division may be possible. More information about the Division, please visit https://amc.hkust.edu.hk/ . Applicants with questions may write to facsearchamc@ust.hk . Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, including annual leave, medical and dental benefits, and housing benefits, will be provided where applicable. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of the contract. Application including (i) a full curriculum vitae; (ii) a statement of teaching; (iii) past teaching records (if applicable) and (iv) three dependent referee information . Applications are accepted at any time and considered on a rolling basis. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187685": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Arts and Machine Creativity Location: Hong Kong The Division of Arts and Machine Creativity (AMC) at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) is among the world’s first academic units dedicated to the intersection of artificial intelligence (AI) and the arts. We invite visionary artists , researchers , and scholars to join us in shaping an innovative environment where technology, art, and the humanities converge to redefine the creative frontier. Why Join AMC? A Leading Global University : HKUST ranks among the world’s top institutions, recognized for academic excellence, groundbreaking research, and impact-driven innovation. Exceptional Students : Our students are talented, curious, and globally minded. Working with them means engaging with motivated learners eager to push creative and technological boundaries. A Groundbreaking Mission : As part of AMC, you will have the unique opportunity to shape the future of this trailblazing division, where your contributions can redefine the landscape of arts and machine creativity. Interdisciplinary Collaboration : Leverage HKUST’s world-class expertise in science, engineering, and AI to enhance your research and artistic practice through transformative collaboration. Areas of Interest We invite applications for substantiation-track faculty positions ( Assistant , Associate , or Full Professor ) in the following areas: Machine Creativity : Computer graphics, computer vision, robotics, etc. Machine-assisted Art Practice : Visual, sound, performing, installation, cinematic arts, etc. Critical Studies on Arts and Machine Creativity : Art history, media theory, philosophy of technology, etc. Art Management : Managerial, legal, and business topics related to AI arts, NFTs, etc. What We Offer : Competitive salary and fringe benefits, including annual leave, medical and dental benefits, and housing support. Opportunities for joint appointments with relevant academic departments, fostering cross-disciplinary collaboration. Initial appointments at Assistant Professor/Associate Professor rank are normally on a three-year contract, with gratuity upon successful completion.  Appointments at Professor rank are on a substantive basis. Demonstrate a proven record of research, creative work, and/or teaching excellence in the targeted areas, especially in linking emerging technologies such as generative AI with artistic practices. Interdisciplinary collaboration is highly valued. A PhD in a relevant discipline is typically required, but candidates with distinguished professional or academic achievements may be considered without this qualification. Please submit the following materials: Full curriculum vitae Statements of research interests and teaching philosophy Letter of interest summarizing your qualifications, expertise, and career goals Contact information of three qualified referees Five representative research papers or creative works Applications are accepted on a rolling basis. More information about AMC is available at https://amc.ust.hk . For inquiries, please contact facsearchamc@ust.hk ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188141": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenured and Tenure-track Faculty Position - 2026",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Management Location: Hong Kong The Department of Management is currently looking for a tenured or tenure-track faculty to join our team and help build a global hub for cutting-edge research in management. Established in 1991, the HKUST Business School is recognized globally as one of the world’s best business schools. Our Executive MBA Program, offered in collaboration with the Kellogg School of Management, was ranked No. 4 in the world in the Financial Times EMBA 2025 ranking. Additionally, our fulltime MBA program was ranked 24th worldwide in the Financial Times Global MBA Ranking 2026. The Department of Management at HKUST aims to be a leading intellectual center for management research and education. The University provides a supportive research and teaching environment with attractive research funding, strong teaching support staff, and leading-edge facilities. The Department has a group of productive faculty members who are enthusiastic about conducting high-quality research, and have regularly published in premier management journals. For more information about our faculty, teaching, current research programs, and research center, please visit our department website . Applications and nominations are now invited for faculty positions at all ranks (tenured and tenure-track) in the micro (e.g., ethics, entrepreneurship, family business, human resource management, and organizational behavior) and macro area (e.g., corporate social responsibilities and sustainability, entrepreneurship, family business, innovation, international management, organization theory, and strategy). Candidates for the assistant professor position should have an earned doctorate in a relevant discipline (upon appointment) and a record of publishing or the potential to publish in premium management journals (e.g., Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Administrative Science Quarterly, Journal of Applied Psychology, Organization Science, and Strategic Management Journal ). Demonstrated capacity for quality teaching is also required. For fresh assistant professors, the teaching load is two courses in the first year and three afterwards. For senior positions, a strong record of published research in premier management journals and a record of teaching in MBA or EMBA programs are required. Appointment with tenure requires a formal review. The language of instruction at HKUST is English. Interested candidates are invited to submit the required materials electronically via Interfolio . Required materials include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae List of references Research statement Teaching statement Teaching records (if available) Three representative writing samples Review of applications for all positions begins on August 20, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled . A special note for those attending this summer's Academy of Management (AOM) Meeting in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, candidates are required to submit a cover letter and CV via Interfolio by July 10, 2026 , to schedule a potential interview."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187269": {
      "title": "AI in Bioscience Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Hong Kong The Division of Life Science at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seeks outstanding candidates for faculty positions in AI in Bioscience , a rapidly evolving frontier that is transforming how biological and biomedical research is conducted. The Division is actively investing in this strategic area to drive next-generation discovery through the integration of artificial intelligence, data science, and life sciences. Candidates will have the opportunity to shape emerging directions at the interface of computation and biology, supported by strong institutional commitment and cutting-edge infrastructure. Research areas of interest include: Development of novel AI and machine learning methodologies for biological and biomedical discovery Advanced computational approaches for large-scale multi‑omics data, biological imaging, and systems biology Predictive modelling and data-driven understanding of complex biological systems and disease mechanisms The Division is recruiting multiple tenure-track and tenured faculty members to advance its mission of understanding the mechanisms underlying human health and disease through both basic and translational research. Outstanding candidates at both junior and senior levels will be considered. Successful applicants are expected to establish independent, internationally competitive research programs and contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. Division of Life Science The Division of Life Science has established strengths across seven thematic areas: (i) Neuroscience and Nervous System Disorders, (ii) Cancer Biology, (iii) Cell Biology and Signaling, (iv) Stem Cell and Developmental Biology, (v) Macromolecular Structure and Function, (vi) Biotechnology and Medicinal Biochemistry, and (vii) Genomics and Epigenomics. These interconnected themes foster extensive cross-disciplinary collaboration across the life sciences. Faculty members are internationally recognized, and the Division is supported by world-class research infrastructure at HKUST, including the Biosciences Central Research Facility , the Biological Cryo-EM Center , the Laboratory Animal Facility , and a state-of-the-art AI Supercomputing Facility . The Division also offers vibrant postgraduate programs and strong global and industry partnerships. HKUST is a globally recognized research university at the forefront of science, engineering, and business. The University is advancing the development of a new, technology-driven Medical School, offering unique opportunities for interdisciplinary and translational research. Beyond academia, HKUST fosters a dynamic innovation ecosystem, including a strong portfolio of start-ups and high-impact ventures. The University is committed to the values of Excellence, Integrity, and Academic Freedom. Applicants should possess: A Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree Completion of postdoctoral training Demonstrated potential to lead an independent, externally funded research program Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae A three-page research statement and a one-page teaching statement Names and contact details of three referees Applicants should submit their application via HKUST recruitment website: https://apply.interfolio.com/187269 (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187268": {
      "title": "Aging and Age‑Related Diseases Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Hong Kong The Division of Life Science at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seeks outstanding candidates for faculty positions in Aging and Age ‑ Related Diseases, a strategic focus that brings together expertise from multiple disciplines to address the biological mechanisms of aging and their links to disease. The Division offers a highly collaborative environment with strong support for interdisciplinary and translational research. We welcome applications from candidates working across molecular to systems-level studies of aging. Areas of particular interest include: Biological mechanisms of aging and longevity Age-associated diseases, including neurodegenerative, metabolic, cardiovascular, and musculoskeletal disorders Integrative approaches spanning cellular, organismal, and systems biology The Division is recruiting multiple tenure-track and tenured faculty members to advance its mission of understanding the mechanisms underlying human health and disease through both basic and translational research. Outstanding candidates at both junior and senior levels will be considered. Successful applicants are expected to establish independent, internationally competitive research programs and contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. Division of Life Science The Division of Life Science has established strengths across seven thematic areas: (i) Neuroscience and Nervous System Disorders, (ii) Cancer Biology, (iii) Cell Biology and Signaling, (iv) Stem Cell and Developmental Biology, (v) Macromolecular Structure and Function, (vi) Biotechnology and Medicinal Biochemistry, and (vii) Genomics and Epigenomics. These interconnected themes foster extensive cross-disciplinary collaboration across the life sciences. Faculty members are internationally recognized, and the Division is supported by world-class research infrastructure at HKUST, including the Biosciences Central Research Facility , the Biological Cryo-EM Center , the Laboratory Animal Facility , and a state-of-the-art AI Supercomputing Facility . The Division also offers vibrant postgraduate programs and strong global and industry partnerships. HKUST is a globally recognized research university at the forefront of science, engineering, and business. The University is advancing the development of a new, technology-driven Medical School, offering unique opportunities for interdisciplinary and translational research. Beyond academia, HKUST fosters a dynamic innovation ecosystem, including a strong portfolio of start-ups and high-impact ventures. The University is committed to the values of Excellence, Integrity, and Academic Freedom. Applicants should possess: A Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree Completion of postdoctoral training Demonstrated potential to lead an independent, externally funded research program Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae A three-page research statement and a one-page teaching statement Names and contact details of three referees Applicants should submit their application via HKUST recruitment website: https://apply.interfolio.com/187268 (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187270": {
      "title": "Drug Discovery and Translational Therapeutics Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Hong Kong The Division of Life Science at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seeks outstanding candidates for faculty positions in Drug Discovery and Translational Therapeutics , a key focus area supported by established strengths in biotechnology and related disciplines. The research environment enables effective translation of fundamental discoveries into therapeutic applications. Research areas include: Target identification and validation Drug discovery, pharmacology, and chemical biology Mechanisms of action and therapeutic pathways Translational pipelines linking discovery to preclinical and clinical development The Division is recruiting multiple tenure-track and tenured faculty members to advance its mission of understanding the mechanisms underlying human health and disease through both basic and translational research. Outstanding candidates at both junior and senior levels will be considered. Successful applicants are expected to establish independent, internationally competitive research programs and contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. Division of Life Science The Division of Life Science has established strengths across seven thematic areas: (i) Neuroscience and Nervous System Disorders, (ii) Cancer Biology, (iii) Cell Biology and Signaling, (iv) Stem Cell and Developmental Biology, (v) Macromolecular Structure and Function, (vi) Biotechnology and Medicinal Biochemistry, and (vii) Genomics and Epigenomics. These interconnected themes foster extensive cross-disciplinary collaboration across the life sciences. Faculty members are internationally recognized, and the Division is supported by world-class research infrastructure at HKUST, including the Biosciences Central Research Facility , the Biological Cryo-EM Center , the Laboratory Animal Facility , and a state-of-the-art AI Supercomputing Facility . The Division also offers vibrant postgraduate programs and strong global and industry partnerships. HKUST is a globally recognized research university at the forefront of science, engineering, and business. The University is advancing the development of a new, technology-driven Medical School, offering unique opportunities for interdisciplinary and translational research. Beyond academia, HKUST fosters a dynamic innovation ecosystem, including a strong portfolio of start-ups and high-impact ventures. The University is committed to the values of Excellence, Integrity, and Academic Freedom. Applicants should possess: A Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree Completion of postdoctoral training Demonstrated potential to lead an independent, externally funded research program Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae A three-page research statement and a one-page teaching statement Names and contact details of three referees Applicants should submit their application via HKUST recruitment website: https://apply.interfolio.com/187270 (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187267": {
      "title": "Neuroscience and Neurological Diseases Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Hong Kong The Division of Life Science at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seeks outstanding candidates for faculty positions in Neuroscience and Neurological Diseases , a strategic priority of both the Division and the University. This area is supported by strong leadership, substantial research investment, and active participation in major collaborative and institute-level initiatives. We invite applications from candidates working in molecular, cellular, systems, or computational neuroscience. Areas of particular interest include: Neurodevelopment and neurodegeneration Neural circuits and brain–body interactions Neurological and neuropsychiatric disorders Computational and data‑driven approaches in neuroscience The Division is recruiting multiple tenure-track and tenured faculty members to advance its mission of understanding the mechanisms underlying human health and disease through both basic and translational research. Outstanding candidates at both junior and senior levels will be considered. Successful applicants are expected to establish independent, internationally competitive research programs and contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. Division of Life Science The Division of Life Science has established strengths across seven thematic areas: (i) Neuroscience and Nervous System Disorders, (ii) Cancer Biology, (iii) Cell Biology and Signaling, (iv) Stem Cell and Developmental Biology, (v) Macromolecular Structure and Function, (vi) Biotechnology and Medicinal Biochemistry, and (vii) Genomics and Epigenomics. These interconnected themes foster extensive cross-disciplinary collaboration across the life sciences. Faculty members are internationally recognized, and the Division is supported by world-class research infrastructure at HKUST, including the Biosciences Central Research Facility , the Biological Cryo-EM Center , the Laboratory Animal Facility , and a state-of-the-art AI Supercomputing Facility . The Division also offers vibrant postgraduate programs and strong global and industry partnerships. HKUST is a globally recognized research university at the forefront of science, engineering, and business. The University is advancing the development of a new, technology-driven Medical School, offering unique opportunities for interdisciplinary and translational research. Beyond academia, HKUST fosters a dynamic innovation ecosystem, including a strong portfolio of start-ups and high-impact ventures. The University is committed to the values of Excellence, Integrity, and Academic Freedom. Applicants should possess: A Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree Completion of postdoctoral training Demonstrated potential to lead an independent, externally funded research program Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae A three-page research statement and a one-page teaching statement Names and contact details of three referees Applicants should submit their application via HKUST recruitment website: https://apply.interfolio.com/187267 (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185568": {
      "title": "Head of the Division of Humanities",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academic: School of Humanities and Social Science Location: Division of Humanities, HKUST, Clear Water Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong SAR HKUST Founded in 1991, HKUST is a publicly funded international university dedicated to undergraduate and postgraduate education and research in science, engineering, business & management, and humanities & social science. We seek to nurture students with entrepreneurial spirit, innovative thinking, and global outlook and strive to work together to make a strong societal impact. The University is ranked as one of the most international universities in Asia comprising four Schools and an Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies and multiple research institutes/central research facilities; and the Hong Kong government has recently endorsed our competitive bid to develop a new Medical School. While actively growing, at present there are around 970 faculty members, and an enrollment of about 11,000 undergraduate and 8,700 postgraduate students. English is the language used in all teaching, research, and administration. HKUST is celebrating its 35th Anniversary this year with a strong presence in global higher education. It has received many international recognitions including citations and rankings; for example, HKUST ranks 6th in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026 , 3rd in the Times Higher Education Young University Rankings 2024 , and 19th globally (1st in Hong Kong) in the Times Higher Education Impact Rankings 2025 . A total of 11 subjects offered by HKUST are ranked among the world’s top 50 in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026 . Moreover, it has consistently been ranked within the world’s top 30 in the Global Employability University Ranking, reflecting the strong competitiveness of its graduates. At the heart of the University’s pursuit of excellence in teaching, research, and societal impact lies uncompromising efforts to recruit and retain the best talents globally and locally. We seek to diversify HKUST’s critical mass of world-class academics, researchers, staff and students in order to drive cutting-edge education and research initiatives and deliver academic and administrative excellence. The University promotes a diverse learning environment that enhances student development of their creativity, innovative thinking and global outlook, especially in today’s rapidly changing society, and technological and AI development. Proactive faculty recruitment is undertaken from around the world in all disciplines of the University. HKUST upholds the values of diversity and an inclusive and collaborative community. The Division of Humanities The Division has a multidisciplinary faculty of 30+ members, specializing in history, literature, film and media studies, linguistics, philosophy and religion, anthropology, and music and creative arts. Directly accountable to the Dean of SHSS, the Head is the chief executive of the Division who is responsible for strategic development, curricular matters, research direction, faculty recruitment as well as resource and personnel management. The Division’s graduate degree programs include an MA in Chinese Culture and MPhil/PhD in Humanities. The Division also participates in the BSc program in Global China Studies and provides humanities education as a common core to all undergraduates at HKUST. Associated with the Division are the Center for Chinese Linguistics and the South China Research Center, in which core faculty from the Division participate. Job Functions The Head provides academic leadership and strategic vision for the Division of Humanities at HKUST. With responsibility for a broad, interdisciplinary Division that is not subdivided into traditional departments, the Head will strengthen dialogue across History, Literature, Film and Media Studies, Linguistics, Philosophy and Religion, Anthropology, and Music and Creative Arts. Reporting to the Dean of the School of Humanities and Social Science, a strong applicant will provide strategic leadership and vision for the Division, including its teaching, research, postgraduate training, public engagement, and future strategic development; promote excellence across the full range of Humanities disciplines represented in the Division, while fostering intellectual dialogue, interdisciplinary collaboration, and mutual respect among different fields; support high-quality undergraduate education for students across HKUST, including those in science, engineering, business and management, by ensuring that Humanities courses cultivate broad cultural understanding, critical inquiry, and global awareness; provide leadership for postgraduate education and research training, ensuring that programs remain rigorous, integrated, and internationally competitive; enhance the Division’s research profile by supporting disciplinary depth, interdisciplinary collaboration, externally funded research, public-facing Humanities initiatives, and emerging opportunities at the interface of the Humanities, digital methods, AI, and society; work collaboratively with faculty, teaching staff, administrative staff, students, the School, and other units of the University to advance shared academic priorities; exercise transparent and inclusive decision-making, with effective communication across the Division and beyond; effectively deploy human, financial, space, and other resources in support of the Division’s academic mission. Terms & Applications/Nominations Appointment to the position of Division Head will be on a three-year fixed term basis, renewable by mutual agreement. The appointee will be considered concurrently for substantiated employment at the Professor or Chair Professor rank. Competitive remuneration and generous fringe benefits, including housing where appropriate, will be provided. Additional information about the University and the Division of Humanities is available on the websites https://hkust.edu.hk/ and https://huma.hkust.edu.hk/ respectively. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in a Humanities discipline or a closely related interdisciplinary field; a distinguished record of academic achievement suitable for appointment at the rank of full professor/chair professor; an international scholarly profile in one or more areas relevant to the Division’s academic scope, such as History, Literature, Film and Media Studies, Linguistics, Philosophy and Religion, Anthropology, and Music and Creative Arts, or related interdisciplinary areas; a strong commitment to the value of Humanities education within a leading science and technology university; demonstrated leadership in curriculum development, research development, postgraduate training, faculty mentoring, or academic program building; appreciation of interdisciplinary and comparative approaches, especially in relation to China, Hong Kong, Asia, and global contexts; administrative capability to lead a diverse academic unit, including experience in resource management, team building, strategic planning, and collegial governance; a commitment to leading an inclusive workplace that recognizes the distinctive contributions of all disciplines and scholarly traditions within the Division; excellent communication skills for use in a multilingual and multicultural academic environment, and with stakeholders within the University, across Hong Kong, and internationally. Applications should be submitted to the School of Humanities and Social Science via Interfolio with (i) a cover letter and (ii) a full CV. Review of applications will start from 4 May 2026 and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185063": {
      "title": "Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor (Robotic Hiring Task Force)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academic: School of Engineering Location: Hong Kong The Cheng Kar-Shun Robotics Institute (CKSRI) ( https://ri.hkust.edu.hk/ )at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) invites applications for substantiation-track faculty positions at the ranks of Professor, Associate Professor, and Assistant Professor for the 2026-2027 academic year. Successful candidates will hold appointments in the appropriate academic departments. We are looking for outstanding candidates in the area of embodied AI and medical robots. Research areas of interest include but are not limited to Control and Autonomy, Embodied AI, Robot Learning, Physical AI, Surgical Robots, Rehabilitation Robots, Healthcare Robots, etc. All candidates must have a PhD degree in Electronic and Computer Engineering, Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering, Computer Science and Engineering, or related fields by the time of appointment. The salary and startup package are highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include medical/dental benefits and annual leave. Housing will also be provided where applicable. Assistant Professor appointments will initially be on a three-year contract. A gratuity will be payable upon completion of the contract. Candidates will be interviewed by appropriate department search committees. HKUST is ranked among the best young universities in the world and is committed to increasing the gender and ethnic diversity of its faculty with a range of family-friendly policies in place. The medium of instruction is English. Application Procedure Applications including 1) a cover letter, 2) a full curriculum vitae, 3) names and contact information of at least three referees, 4) a research statement, and 5) a teaching statement (all in PDF format) should be submitted via the HKUST Recruitment System. Applicants should first sign up to create a personal account. Priority will be given to applications received by 30 September 2026. Please be advised that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. (Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11139&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Quantum Science and Technology",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Quantum Science and Technology Job Title: 11139 Job ID: Department: Department of Physics Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Physics at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology invites applications for several tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level. We seek candidates in all areas of quantum science and technology including, but not limited to, quantum information, photonics, quantum optics, cold atoms, neutral atoms, trapped ions, solid state qubits and quantum simulation . An applicant must possess a PhD degree in physics or related field and demonstrate a strong track record of research in quantum science and technology. Appointments at the rank of Associate Professor level or above will also be considered for candidates with exceptional records of research excellence and academic leadership. In addition to pursuing a vibrant research program, an appointee will be expected to engage in effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Starting salary will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits, annual leave and housing benefits will be provided where applicable. The initial appointment prior to tenure will normally be on three-year contract terms. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a contract. Further information about the Department is available at https://physics.hkust.edu.hk/ . Application Procedure Applicants should submit their application including CV, cover letter, complete publication list, research statement, teaching statement, and at least three reference letters, via AcademicJobsOnline.Org at [ https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/30878] . (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11138&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Theoretical and Computational Physics",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Theoretical and Computational Physics Job Title: 11138 Job ID: Department: Department of Physics Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Physics at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology invites applications for several tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level. We seek candidates in several areas of theoretical and computational physics including, but not limited to, statistical physics (including AI related physics) and large-scale simulation of quantum many-body systems . An applicant must possess a PhD degree in physics or related field and demonstrate a strong track record of research in theoretical and/or computational physics. Appointments at the rank of Associate Professor or above will also be considered for candidates with exceptional records of research excellence and academic leadership. In addition to pursuing a vibrant research program, an appointee will be expected to engage in effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Starting salary will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits, annual leave and housing benefits will be provided where applicable. The initial appointment prior to tenure will normally be on three-year contract terms. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a contract. Further information about the Department is available at https://physics.hkust.edu.hk/ . Application Procedure Applicants should submit their application including CV, cover letter, complete publication list, research statement, teaching statement, and at least three reference letters, via AcademicJobsOnline.Org at [ https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/30879 ] (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11137&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics Job Title: 11137 Job ID: Department: Department of Physics Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Physics at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology invites applications for several tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level. We seek candidates in all areas of experimental condensed matter physics including, but not limited to, quantum materials and devices, light-matter interactions, material fabrication and advanced characterization, soft condensed matter . An applicant must possess a PhD degree in physics or related field and demonstrate a strong track record of research in experimental condensed matter physics. Appointment at Associate Professor level or above will also be considered for candidates with exceptional records of research excellence and academic leadership. In addition to pursuing a vibrant research program, an appointee will be expected to engage in effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Starting salary will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits, annual leave and housing benefits will be provided where applicable. The initial appointment prior to tenure will normally be on three-year contract terms. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a contract. Further information about the Department is available at https://physics.hkust.edu.hk/ . Application Procedure Applicants should submit their application including CV, cover letter, complete publication list, research statement, teaching statement, and at least three reference letters, via AcademicJobsOnline.Org at [ https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/29807 ] (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11136&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Theoretical Particle Physics and Cosmology",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Theoretical Particle Physics and Cosmology Job Title: 11136 Job ID: Department: Department of Physics Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Physics invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level in Theoretical Particle Physics and Cosmology . An applicant must possess a PhD degree in physics or related field and demonstrate a strong track record of research in theoretical particle physics and/or cosmology . Appointments at the rank of Associate Professor or above will also be considered for candidates with exceptional records of research excellence and academic leadership. In addition to pursuing a vibrant research program, an appointee will be expected to engage in effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The current faculty in the particle physics and cosmology group at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology include Professors Andrew Cohen, Tao Liu, Kam-Biu Luk, Kirill Prokofiev, Yi Wang and Yue Zhao. The department is expanding its effort in this area by hiring new faculty in theory and experiment. Further information about the Department can be found at https://physics.hkust.edu.hk/ . Starting salary will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits, annual leave and housing benefits will be provided where applicable. The initial appointment prior to tenure will normally be on three-year contract terms. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a contract. Application Procedure Applicants should submit their application including CV, cover letter, complete publication list, research statement, teaching statement, and at least three reference letters, via AcademicJobsOnline.Org at [ https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/29808 ] (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11135&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Observational Cosmology",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Observational Cosmology Job Title: 11135 Job ID: Department: Department of Physics Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Physics invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level in Observational Cosmology. An applicant must possess a PhD degree in physics or related field and demonstrate a strong track record of research in observational cosmology . Appointments at the rank of Associate Professor or above will also be considered for candidates with exceptional records of research excellence and academic leadership. In addition to pursuing a vibrant research program an appointee will be expected to engage in effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The current faculty in the particle physics and cosmology group at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology include Professors Andrew Cohen, Tao Liu, Kam-Biu Luk, Kirill Prokofiev, Yi Wang and Yue Zhao. The department is expanding its effort in this area by hiring new faculty in theory and experiment. Further information about the Department can be found at https://physics.hkust.edu.hk/ . Starting salary will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits, annual leave and housing benefits will be provided where applicable. The initial appointment prior to tenure will normally be on three-year contract terms. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a contract. Application Procedure Applicants should submit their application including CV, cover letter, complete publication list, research statement, teaching statement, and at least three reference letters, via AcademicJobsOnline.Org at [ https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/29810 ] (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11134&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Experimental Particle Physics",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Experimental Particle Physics Job Title: 11134 Job ID: Department: Department of Physics Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Physics invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level in Experimental Particle Physics . An applicant must possess a PhD degree in physics or related field and demonstrate a strong track record of research in particle physics, especially in instrumentation. Appointments at the rank of Associate Professor or above will also be considered for candidates with exceptional records of research excellence and academic leadership. In addition to pursuing a vibrant research program, an appointee will be expected to engage in effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The current faculty in the particle physics and cosmology group at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology include Professors Andrew Cohen, Tao Liu, Kam-Biu Luk, Kirill Prokofiev, Yi Wang and Yue Zhao. The department is expanding its effort in this area by hiring new faculty in theory and experiment. Further information about the Department can be found at https://physics.hkust.edu.hk/ . Starting salary will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits, annual leave and housing benefits will be provided where applicable. The initial appointment prior to tenure will normally be on three-year contract terms. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a contract. Application Procedure Applicants should submit their application including CV, cover letter, complete publication list, research statement, teaching statement, and at least three reference letters, via AcademicJobsOnline.Org at [ https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/29809 ] (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179626": {
      "title": "Faculty positions in Electronic and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academic: School of Engineering: Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering Location: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology The Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering (ECE) at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions at Professor, Associate Professor and Assistant Professor ranks.  The Department comprises faculty conducting research in frontier technologies in a wide scope of fields including biomedical engineering, microelectronics, integrated circuits and systems, photonics, control and robotic systems, data science and artificial intelligence (AI), quantum engineering, and wireless communications and networking. The Department is interested in outstanding candidates in all ECE-related areas and particularly in control and robotic systems; microelectronics and photonics; networking; and quantum engineering. The School of Engineering at HKUST has launched an aggressive global search to attract internationally renowned scholars and their teams to work in Hong Kong. The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology is a world-renowned research university in Asia’s most vibrant city, Hong Kong.  According to THE World University Rankings by Subject - Engineering and Technology in 2025, HKUST is ranked #33 in the world. Its Engineering School offers outstanding opportunities and state-of-the-art facilities for faculty and students to pursue innovative research in diverse disciplines within an essentially a north-American education system. English is the medium of teaching, research and administration. The Department has about 50 faculty members, 600 undergraduate students and over 300 postgraduate students. It provides an excellent environment for multidisciplinary research, with close links to other departments within the School of Engineering and to other Schools through joint appointments and active involvements in cross-cutting Institutes and Centers in Quantum Technology, Robotics, Artificial Intelligence, Big Data, and Energy. More information about the Department is available at: https://ece.hkust.edu.hk . Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Fringe benefits include medical/dental benefits and annual leave.  Housing benefits, including on-campus housing, will be provided where applicable.  Substantial support is also provided to faculty in terms of first-rate research facilities, equipment, and research postgraduate studentships.  For appointment at Assistant Professor level, the initial appointment will normally be on a three-year contract.  A gratuity will be payable upon completion of the contract. Applicants must have an PhD degree with demonstrated strength in research and commitment to teaching. Successful candidates are expected to lead active research programs and to teach both graduate and undergraduate courses.  An interdisciplinary knowledge and application of different disciplines will be an advantage. Applications including 1) a cover letter, 2) a full curriculum vitae and a list of publications, 3) names of three referees, and 4) a research proposal and a teaching statement must be submitted through the HKUST recruitment system at this link: https://apply.interfolio.com/179626. The applicants must first sign up to create a personal account.  Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and candidates are strongly encouraged to submit applications as soon as possible and applications will be considered until the openings are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11095&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Biomedical Sciences Faculty",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Biomedical Sciences Faculty Job Title: 11095 Job ID: Department: HKUST School of Medicine Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) invites applications from exceptional candidates for biomedical sciences faculty positions (Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor) for its new School of Medicine. The University HKUST is a dynamic young University with a global reputation for impact and innovation. Founded in 1991, HKUST is consistently ranked among the world’s best institutions and 1st in Hong Kong for graduate employability. As a world-renowned international research and interdisciplinary University with top-tier programs in science, engineering, business and management, humanities and social science, and interdisciplinary studies, HKUST is known for its entrepreneurial culture and powerful connections to industry and research. The University’s English-speaking academic community thrives in a world-class, scenic environment at the Clear Water Bay campus. HKUST’s pioneering spirit is amplified through the “Unified HKUST, Complementary Campuses” framework, expanded by the opening of the innovative HKUST(Guangzhou) campus in 2022, which deepens its interdisciplinary reach into the Greater Bay Area and beyond. For more information about HKUST, please visit: https://hkust.edu.hk . The HKUST School of Medicine HKUST is embarking on a landmark initiative to establish the third medical school of Hong Kong following the successful proposal of the University and subsequent official approval from the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government. The HKUST School of Medicine aspires to be a transformative force, focused on world-class education and research while attracting global talents. By integrating cutting-edge technology and pioneering science, the School will help shape the future of medicine and reinforce Hong Kong’s position as an international hub for medical training, research, and innovation. Built upon HKUST’s interdisciplinary strengths, deeply international character, and global networks, the School will foster a world-class learning environment. As a leader in fields such as artificial intelligence, data science, and robotics, HKUST is uniquely positioned to create a medical school that fuses exceptional clinical expertise with technological innovation. Its mission is to cultivate future-ready physicians who are not only clinically outstanding but also technologically adept, innovative, and compassionate. The School will launch a 4-year graduate-entry Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery (MBBS) program, with global admissions opening by 2027 and the inaugural class expected to commence in the 2028/29 academic year. The School will initially operate in a dedicated new medical teaching and research building at the Clear Water Bay campus, along with satellite site(s) close to a teaching hospital partner. Its long-term future includes a transition to a permanent, integrated campus and medical teaching and research hospital within Hong Kong's strategic Northern Metropolis, placing it at the center of the dynamic Greater Bay Area innovation ecosystem. About the Roles We invite applications from outstanding individuals with a strong commitment to both research and medical education. Appointees will contribute to pre-clinical teaching and postgraduate supervision, alongside a vibrant research program that advances biomedical science and its application to medicine. We offer a dynamic and collaborative environment with state-of-the-art facilities, fostering excellence and innovation in advancing healthcare. Faculty members will have ample opportunities to develop cutting-edge curricula, engage in pioneering research, and shape the future of medical practice in the region. Candidates Applicants should have: A PhD and/or MD degree in biology, biomedical sciences, medicine, or a closely related area. A strong track record in both research and teaching, with demonstrated excellence in the relevant area. A demonstrated commitment to knowledge exchange, teamwork, and international engagement. Experience in medical education will be viewed favorably. Applicants for Professor or Associate Professor should have substantial experience and a distinguished record of research excellence and academic leadership. A strong record of publication in leading journals and success in obtaining competitive external funding are expected. Applicants with less experience will be considered for Assistant Professor positions. Terms of Appointment Appointment as Professor will be on a substantive (tenured) basis. Initial appointment for Associate Professor / Assistant Professor will normally be on a 3-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. Strong candidates applying for an Associate Professor position may be considered for appointment on substantive terms. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, and housing benefits (where applicable). Application Procedure Interested candidates should apply online ( https://hkustcareers.ust.hk ), submitting: (a) an up-to-date curriculum vitae; (b) a one-page summary describing their most outstanding accomplishments and qualifications; (c) a statement of teaching philosophy; (d) a one-page description of their future research and career plan; and (e) the names and contact details of three referees (including email addresses). Review of applications will begin immediately until the positions are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement ( https://hro.hkust.edu.hk/rcpics ) before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11094&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Clinical Faculty Job Title: 11094 Job ID: Department: HKUST School of Medicine Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) invites applications from exceptional candidates for clinical faculty positions (Clinical Professor / Clinical Associate Professor / Clinical Assistant Professor) for its new School of Medicine, in a range of clinical disciplines including but not limited to: Medicine / Surgery / Orthopaedics and Traumatology / Obstetrics and Gynaecology / Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine / Family Medicine / Psychiatry / and others such as Community Medicine / Geriatric Medicine / Emergency Medicine / Radiology / Oncology / Pathology The University HKUST is a dynamic young University with a global reputation for impact and innovation. Founded in 1991, HKUST is consistently ranked among the world’s best institutions and 1st in Hong Kong for graduate employability. As a world-renowned international research and interdisciplinary University with top-tier programs in science, engineering, business and management, humanities and social science, and interdisciplinary studies, HKUST is known for its entrepreneurial culture and powerful connections to industry and research. The University’s English-speaking academic community thrives in a world-class, scenic environment at the Clear Water Bay campus. HKUST’s pioneering spirit is amplified through the “Unified HKUST, Complementary Campuses” framework, expanded by the opening of the innovative HKUST(Guangzhou) campus in 2022, which deepens its interdisciplinary reach into the Greater Bay Area and beyond. For more information about HKUST, please visit: https://hkust.edu.hk . The HKUST School of Medicine HKUST is embarking on a landmark initiative to establish the third medical school of Hong Kong following the successful proposal of the University and subsequent official approval from the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government. The HKUST School of Medicine aspires to be a transformative force, focused on world-class education and research while attracting global talents. By integrating cutting-edge technology and pioneering science, the School will help shape the future of medicine and reinforce Hong Kong’s position as an international hub for medical training, research, and innovation. Built upon HKUST’s interdisciplinary strengths, deeply international character, and global networks, the School will foster a world-class learning environment. As a leader in fields such as artificial intelligence, data science, and robotics, HKUST is uniquely positioned to create a medical school that fuses exceptional clinical expertise with technological innovation. Its mission is to cultivate future-ready physicians who are not only clinically outstanding but also technologically adept, innovative, and compassionate. The School will launch a 4-year graduate-entry Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery (MBBS) program, with global admissions opening by 2027 and the inaugural class expected to commence in the 2028/29 academic year. The School will initially operate in a dedicated new medical teaching and research building at the Clear Water Bay campus, along with satellite site(s) close to a teaching hospital partner. Its long-term future includes a transition to a permanent, integrated campus and medical teaching and research hospital within Hong Kong's strategic Northern Metropolis, placing it at the center of the dynamic Greater Bay Area innovation ecosystem. About the Roles This is an invitation to join as the inaugural batch of clinical faculty of Hong Kong’s third medical school, at HKUST – a unique opportunity to integrate clinical education and research with world-leading strengths in artificial intelligence, data science, and the biomedical sciences and engineering, bringing long-term impact on health care in Hong Kong and beyond. We are seeking visionary clinician-educators and physician-scientists to shape the School from its inception, actively contributing to its direction and growth. Appointees will play an active role in medical student education, including curriculum design and program accreditation, and will help pioneer innovative, technology-driven pedagogies. A deep commitment to research is central to the School’s mission; physician-scientists will lead cutting-edge clinical and translational research that pushes boundaries and drives the development of novel diagnostics, therapeutics, and healthcare technologies. Eligible appointees may also provide clinical services through the University’s public and private health service partners, ensuring synergy between clinical practice, teaching and research. Candidates Applicants should have: A medical qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong, with a specialist qualification (or comparable overseas qualification) recognized by the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine. Limited registration will be arranged for eligible overseas candidates. A higher academic qualification (e.g., MD, MS, PhD) is highly advantageous. Demonstrated clinical excellence and professional expertise in their field. A strong commitment to, and proven experience in, effective teaching of medical students, interns, and trainees, with a vision for integrating technology into education. A demonstrated capacity to initiate and contribute to basic, clinical, and/or translational research, with a strong ethos for fostering interdisciplinary collaborations. A strong record of peer-reviewed publications and a trajectory for securing competitive research funding are expected. Applicants for Clinical Professor or Clinical Associate Professor should have substantial experience and a distinguished record of clinical and/or research achievement, leadership in education and research, and a regional/international reputation in their field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for Clinical Assistant Professor positions. Types of Appointments Recognizing the diverse strengths of exceptional faculty, the School offers two distinct career paths: Clinical Professoriate Track: For appointees with a higher proportion of teaching and research duties, focusing on both educational and research leadership. Clinical Professoriate of Practice Track: For appointees with a higher proportion of teaching and clinical service duties, focusing on clinical excellence and the integration of practice into education. Appointment as Clinical Professor will be on a substantive basis. Initial appointment for Clinical Associate Professor / Clinical Assistant Professor will normally be on a 3-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. Strong candidates applying for a Clinical Associate Professor position may be considered for appointment on substantive terms. Appointments on the Clinical Professoriate of Practice track will be on a 3-year renewable contract. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits, and housing benefits (where applicable). Application Procedure Interested candidates should apply online ( https://hkustcareers.ust.hk ), submitting: (a) an up-to-date curriculum vitae; (b) a one-page summary describing their most outstanding accomplishments and qualifications; (c) a statement of teaching philosophy; (d) a one-page description of their future research and career plan; and (e) the names and contact details of three referees (including email addresses). Review of applications will begin immediately until the positions are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement ( https://hro.hkust.edu.hk/rcpics ) before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11081&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Positions Job Title: 11081 Job ID: Department: Division of Integrative Systems and Design Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Division of Integrative Systems and Design (ISD) strives to study and promote leadership in the design and creation of innovative products and systems. We support cross-disciplinary research projects. The specific research areas of interest include design theory, digital technology and society, smart society, robotics and AI, IoT for integrative system, modelling, simulation and verification technology for integrative systems design as well as design for cross disciplinary research. Applicants should have a PhD degree in engineering, design or a closely related field. Successful candidates are expected to develop strong, independent and innovative programs of externally sponsored research; contribute to both undergraduate and graduate teaching across the Division, as well as participate in services of the Division, the Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies and the University. About ISD in HKUST The Division aspires to nurture a new generation of innovators who can work across multiple disciplines and create disruptive innovations. The vision of ISD is to 1) provide state-of-the-art project-based experiential learning in design education and 2) be a cradle for nurturing innovators and researchers with a design and system thinking mindset as well as an entrepreneurial spirit. The Division provides comprehensive teaching and research programs in integrated design and systems thinking. The academic degrees offered by ISD are a BSc in Innovation, Design and Technology, a MSc in Technology Leadership & Entrepreneurship, a MPhil degree in Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship and a PhD and MPhil programs in Integrative Systems and Design. We are expanding rapidly and looking to broaden into disciplines such as sports, marine technology and medical technology. The Division provides an excellent home for faculty and students that are multi-disciplinary and inclined strongly to an experiential learning mindset. We encourage any potential candidates to visit the ISD webpage at https://isd.hkust.edu.hk to get a better sense of the diverse range of interests and projects of our current faculty. HKUST is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty and has a range of family-friendly policies in place. Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits and housing benefits. Appointment for Professor will be on substantive basis. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor/Associate Professor will normally be on a 3-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Strong candidates applying for an Associate Professor position may also be considered for appointment on substantive terms. Application Procedure Applications with (i) a full curriculum vitae, (ii) a statement of research and teaching, (iii) a list of publications, and (iv) names, emails and addresses of three referees, should be directed to the Search and Appointment Committee by email to isdsearch@ust.hk . Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the positions are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=11015&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Positions Job Title: 11015 Job ID: Department: Department of Chemistry Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Chemistry at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology invites applications for faculty positions in all areas of chemistry and at all ranks. We especially encourage applications in medicinal chemistry, bioanalytical chemistry, chemical biology, inorganic chemistry, and computational chemistry focused on biological systems. Appointees are expected to teach chemistry courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and to develop a vigorous research program in their areas of interest. Applicants should have a PhD degree in Chemistry or a related discipline, and ideally with two years’ post-doctoral research experience. Additional information about the openings, and the University and the Department can be found at https://hkust.edu.hk and https://chem.hkust.edu.hk respectively. Starting salaries will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical/ dental package and annual leave will be provided. Housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. Initial appointment at Assistant Professor/Associate Professor rank will normally be made on a 3-year contract. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Appointment at Professor rank will be on a substantive basis. Application Procedure Applications should be sent to the Chair of the Chemistry Search Committee, Department of Chemistry, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology, Clear Water Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong, by email to facsearchem@ust.hk. Application packages should include a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, an original research proposal, and the names and contact details of three referees (including email addresses). Review of applications will commence in October 2025 and will continue until the positions are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=10912&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Position",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Position Job Title: 10912 Job ID: Department: Division of Public Policy Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details Founded in 1991, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) is a world-renowned international research university dedicated to the advancement of learning and scholarship, with special emphasis on postgraduate education and close collaboration with the industry and business. HKUST has been ranked among the top world universities by QS university rankings and Times Higher Education for the past five years. English is the medium of teaching, research, and administration. The Division of Public Policy (PPOL) is inviting applications for all rank. Candidates should be well-qualified and accomplished scholars who hold a relevant PhD degree with teaching and research experience in public administration, management, public policy, and other relevant fields. Successful candidates should have a relevant PhD degree, preferably with at least 2 years of post-doctoral experience in relevant fields, such as public policy, public administration, political science. Applicants in the following three research areas: (i) Science, Technology (Innovation) policy; (ii) Social and Urban Policy; (iii) Public Policy and Governance for Emerging Technologies are especially welcome. Proven capacity to interact effectively with government, industry, and commercial sectors would be an advantage. For more information about the University and the Division of Public Policy, please visit https://hkust.edu.hk , and https://ppol.hkust.hk . Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits. Housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. Appointment at Professor rank will be on substantive basis. Initial appointment at the Assistant Professor/Associate Professor rank will normally be made on a three-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Application Procedure To facilitate an official application process, the University requires applicant to submit an application via the central HKUST Recruitment System ( https://facrecruit.hkust.edu.hk/ ). Applicant will need to first sign up to create a personal account via the “ HKUST Hong Kong Campus ”. At the section of “ Academic unit/priority area ”, applicant please select “ Division of Public Policy ” or “ PPOL ”. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=10407&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Founding Head of the Division of Arts and Machine Creativity (AMC)",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Founding Head of the Division of Arts and Machine Creativity (AMC) Job Title: 10407 Job ID: Department: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) established the Division of Arts ad Machine Creativity (AMC) in July 2024 under the Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies (AIS), the fifth school of HKUST. As an interdisciplinary academic unit, AMC aims to be a leading center where technology, art, and humanities converge to drive creativity and innovation. We are seeking a high-caliber academic administrator to lead this new Division as the Founding Head. The Role Reporting to the Dean of AIS, the Founding Head will provide leadership and manage the Division's academic and administrative functions. Key responsibilities include advancing interdisciplinary teaching and research, faculty recruitment, and resource management. The Head will also develop strategies to promote the Division and facilitate interdisciplinary collaboration within HKUST and externally with arts organizations, as well as private, governmental, and non-governmental entities. The Candidate Applicants should be distinguished scholars or artists with outstanding academic and/or professional accomplishments, consistent with an appointment as Full Professor with tenure or equivalent. While a background in the arts is preferred, expertise in art technology and other related areas will be considered. Prior administrative experience is highly desirable. Candidates should demonstrate proven leadership, managerial capabilities, experience in leading collaborative programs, and success in securing external funding. The ability to engage effectively with arts organizations, government, industry, and commercial sectors is advantageous. The Division The Division of Arts and Machine Creativity (AMC) is an interdisciplinary academic unit envisioned as a pioneering center where technology, art, and humanities drive creativity and innovation. This initiative fosters a fusion of innovation and humanities, supporting HKUST’s Strategic Plan 2031 as a major effort to expand academic frontiers through, aiming to lead positive changes in education and research, and empower the next generation to address global challenges. The mission of the Division includes: Bridging the gap between technology and art, by providing students and researchers with professional education and robust environment. Cultivating artistic and creative talents equipped with the skills and knowledge to leverage emerging technologies such as AI and machine learning. Fostering a cross-disciplinary environment that empowers collaboration and innovation among artists and technologists. Developing cutting-edge, interdisciplinary research and education programs in partnership with other institutions in the fields of arts and machine learning AMC’s focus areas include: (a) digital art practice (including visual, sound, performing, installation, cinematic arts); (b) machine creativity; (c) art management covering managerial, legal, and business topics related to AI arts, NFT, etc.; and (d) critical studies examining art history, media theory, and philosophy of technology in the context of arts and machine creativity. The Division will offer graduate degree programs, including MA and MFA programs, as well as MPhil/PhD programs. It will also provide common core courses for all undergraduates at HKUST, and potentially undergraduate programs in future. The Division will collaborate with the Computational Media and Arts Thrust of HKUST(GZ) to advance scientific research in artificial intelligence in generative creativity and machine creativity. The University Founded in 1991, HKUST is a world-renowned international research university dedicated to the advancement of learning, research, scholarship, and the education of a new generation of elite students through top-tier programs in science, engineering, business & management, humanities & social science, and interdisciplinary studies. HKUST is deeply committed to advancing humanities and arts education and research. The School of Humanities and Social Science offers diverse music and creative writing courses led by distinguished artists and active practitioners. Courses include “Music of the World”, “Introduction to Music Composition”, and “Chinese Creative Writing”, fostering creativity and collaboration. Additionally, film courses like “Independent Cinema in Contemporary China” are offered, broadening students' artistic perspectives. Since it was founded 33 years ago, HKUST has already established a strong presence in global higher education and received a number of international recognitions. Among others, HKUST was ranked No.3 in the Times Higher Education’s Young University Rankings 2024, 12 of its subjects were ranked among the world’s top 50 in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2024. While the University is deeply rooted in Hong Kong, HKUST (GZ) in Guangzhou, Mainland China complements the well-established disciplinary foundation at the Hong Kong campus with 4 transdisciplinary hubs and 16 thrust areas. We are dedicated to educating well-rounded students with strong entrepreneurial spirits and innovative and globally oriented thinking. English is the medium of teaching, research, and administration at HKUST. HKUST promotes diversity with an inclusive and collaborative community and the use of modern instructional methods. Terms & Applications The appointment will be concurrent with a substantive professorial appointment. The headship will be a full-time appointment for an initial term of three years, and renewable for another term, subject to further review. HKUST provides competitive remuneration and generous fringe benefits, including housing where appropriate. Application, including a curriculum vitae, a vision statement, as well as names and email addresses of at least three referees, should be sent to the AMC Head Search Committee (c/o Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies), the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology, Clearwater Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong (or by email: amcdhsearch@ust.hk ). Review of applications will begin from early December 2024 and continue until the position is filled. For more information about the University, the Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies and the AMC Division, please visit https://hkust.edu.hk/ and https://ais.hkust.edu.hk/ respectively. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=10148&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Head and Professor of Management",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Head and Professor of Management Job Title: 10148 Job ID: Department: Department of Management Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The School of Business and Management of The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST Business School) ( https://bm.hkust.edu.hk/ ) is seeking a senior academic for the post of Head and Professor of Management at the rank of Full Professor. The University Founded in 1991, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) ( https://hkust.edu.hk/ ) is a world-class university that excels in driving innovative education, research excellence, and impactful knowledge transfer. The University comprises over 800 faculty members whose research activities span a diverse range of disciplines, including science, engineering, business, humanities, and social sciences. With a holistic and interdisciplinary pedagogy approach, HKUST was ranked No.3 in the Times Higher Education’s Young University Rankings 2024, while 12 of its subjects were ranked among the world’s top 50 in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2024. Our graduates are highly competitive, consistently ranking among the world’s top 30 most sought-after employees. In terms of research and entrepreneurship, over 80% of our work was rated “Internationally excellent” or “world leading” in the latest Research Assessment Exercise 2020 of Hong Kong’s University Grants Committee. As of June 2024, HKUST members have founded 1,747 active start-ups, including 10 Unicorns and 14 exits (IPO or M&A). The School and the Department The HKUST Business School has risen to international prominence in a relatively short period of time, achieving widespread global recognition and a variety of prestigious academic rankings. Our strength lies in our full range of program offerings, high-quality research conducted by world-class faculty, and diverse and high-caliber student body. Our research has been ranked No.1 in Asia and No.28 in the world by the University of Texas at Dallas (UTD) Top 100 Business School Research Rankings in the most recent 2019-2023 ranking cycle. Our Executive MBA Program, offered jointly with the Kellogg School of Management, has been ranked 12 times No.1 in the world by the Financial Times, while the HKUST MBA Program has been ranked Top-20 13 times. The Department of Management at HKUST ( https://mgmt.hkust.edu.hk/ ) aims to continue as a leading intellectual center for research in all areas of management, both at the macro (strategy, organizational theory, entrepreneurship, international business) and the micro (organizational behavior, human resource management) levels. It comprises a collegial and diverse group of faculty members regularly publishing in leading journals such as Administrative Science Quarterly, Academy of Management Journal, Organization Science, Strategic Management Journal, and Journal of Applied Psychology, among others. The research output has been ranked as first in Asia, and 33rd in the world by the 2018-2022 UTD ranking. The department offers high-quality programs at the undergraduate, MSc, and PhD levels. The Role Reporting to the Dean of Business and Management, the Head and Professor of Management is expected to provide leadership and manage the Department of Management in its diverse academic and administrative functions. Applications/nominations for the position are invited from well-qualified and accomplished scholars. A qualified candidate is expected to have an outstanding academic record in a major field of management, an international research reputation, and some relevant administrative experience. Terms & Applications/ N ominations: The appointment will be concurrent with a substantive professorial appointment. Upon completion of the headship term, the appointee is expected to continue to commit to the long-term development of the Department. Competitive remuneration and generous fringe benefits, including housing where appropriate, will be provided. HKUST is being represented by Heidrick & Struggles for this search. Applications/nominations, together with full curriculum vitae and the names and addresses/fax numbers/email addresses of referees, should be sent to hkust-mgmt@heidrick.com . Review of candidates will begin immediately and the search will continue until the position is filled. Applications and nominations will be treated in strict confidence. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=9660&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Sustainability",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Positions in Sustainability Job Title: 9660 Job ID: Department: Division of Environment and Sustainability Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Division of Environment and Sustainability at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology is seeking applicants for substantiation-track faculty positions at all ranks (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor) whose scholarly interests cross multiple areas of sustainability and sustainable development. The successful candidates will contribute to the University’s sustainability education strategy by contributing leadership, energy, and vision to a well-balanced and multi-disciplinary approach to understanding key sustainability concepts, principles, theories, and practice. To facilitate a multidisciplinary emphasis, the candidates are expected to have or to generate an internationally recognized research program that stresses collaborative research on solving some of the world’s “wicked” problems – i.e., climate change mitigation and adaptation, smart city, urban planning, food system imbalances, social and economic inequality, technology or governance innovations; and on environmental risk analysis. Candidates should have a strong understanding of experiential “hands-on” learning as a means of instruction for students, and an exemplary teaching record. Successful applicants will be expected to participate in or lead collaborative teams and interdisciplinary research on sustainability and resilience topics. The Division of Environment and Sustainability is an interdisciplinary academic unit dedicated to the use and management of natural resources in an economically efficient, environmentally compatible, and socially responsible manner. Our faculty members publish broadly in both disciplinary journals and diverse, environmentally focused outlets, and are rewarded for working on interdisciplinary teams in applied contexts. Depending on the candidate’s areas of expertise, a joint appointment between the Division of Environment and Sustainability and a relevant academic Department/Division may be possible. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in science, engineering, or an interdisciplinary environmental or natural resources-related program with a focus on these areas. The candidates should have proven teaching and advising experience at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, a strong research and publication record consistent with the candidate’s academic rank, evidence of potential for securing research funding, and a demonstrated ability to work in interdisciplinary teams involving both social and natural scientists. Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits. Housing benefits will be provided where applicable. Appointment at the Professor rank will be on a substantive basis. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor/Associate Professor will normally be made on a 3-year contract. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Application Procedure Application materials including (i) full curriculum vitae; (ii) separate statements of research interests and teaching philosophy; (iii) a letter of interest summarizing your qualifications, areas of expertise and career goals; and (iv) contact information of three qualified referees should be sent in PDF format to envrjob@ust.hk . Review of applications will start in early March 2024 and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=9419&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching-track Faculty Position",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Teaching-track Faculty Position Job Title: 9419 Job ID: Department: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management (ISOM) at HKUST School of Business and Management invites applications for a teaching-track faculty position (Senior Lecturer, Lecturer I or Lecturer II) in Operations Management, expected to begin in July 2024. Titles of Assistant or Associate Professor of Business Education may be offered if appropriate. Candidates should have a PhD degree (or near completion) in Operations Management or other closely related disciplines, and have a strong record or demonstrate a strong competence in both teaching and applied research. The Operations Management group of the department offers undergraduate, MSc and PhD programs, and offers courses for the school’s MBA, EMBA, and DBA programs. The department web site is http://www.bm.ust.hk/~isom . Starting salary will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including annual leave and medical/dental benefits will be provided. Housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. Initial appointment will normally be on a two-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. A gratuity will be payable upon completion of contract. Application Procedure To apply, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), teaching evaluation and two selected research papers, and arrange three reference letters to: Recruitment Committee of Operations Management Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology Clear Water Bay, Kowloon HONG KONG Email: omrecruit@ust.hk Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=9320&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Positions Job Title: 9320 Job ID: Department: Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering (CBE) at HKUST achieved the highest overall rating of 4-star (world-leading research) category in the recent Research Assessment Exercise (RAE 2020) in the area of Chemical and Biomedical Engineering in Hong Kong. To strengthen the strategic areas of the Department, we are now inviting applications for multiple substantiation-track faculty positions at all ranks (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor) in biological engineering (in particular, in the areas of synthetic biology, systems biology, biomedical devices, wearable bioelectronics, and health informatics ); and chemical engineering (in particular, in the areas of functional materials, energy conversion and storage, green catalysis, food technology, process system engineering, data science, and artificial intelligence for medicine and chemical engineering ). Applicants should have a PhD degree in chemical engineering, bioengineering or a closely related field. Successful candidates are expected to develop strong, independent and innovative programs of externally sponsored research; teach effectively in chemical and/or biological engineering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and participate in services of the Department, the School and the University. Details about the Department and its current research activities are available at https://cbe.hkust.edu.hk . For further information about the School of Engineering and the University, please visit https://seng.hkust.edu.hk and https://hkust.edu.hk respectively. Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits. Housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. Appointment for Professor will be on substantive basis. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor/Associate Professor will normally be on a 3-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Strong candidates applying for an Associate Professor position may also be considered for appointment on substantive basis. Application Procedure Interested candidates are invited to upload a full curriculum vitae, statements of research and teaching, and three reference letters (to be submitted online by the referees through the site) via this link: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/23970 . For enquiries, please send them to cbesearch@ust.hk . Review of applications will start immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=8431&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Positions Job Title: 8431 Job ID: Department: Various Departments Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details HKUST Strategic Hiring 2023 Faculty Positions ( https://hkust.edu.hk/ ) Established in 1991, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) is a globally recognized University and contributes both locally and internationally to talent development, new knowledge generation and societal interests. The University was founded on the principle that education, original scholarship, and the development of society are integrally linked and best pursued together. It has the objective of becoming a world leading University with significant international impact and strong local commitment. In relentless pursuit of excellence, it leads the advance of and education in science, technology, business, humanities and social science. Celebrating its 30 th birthday during the most challenging time in the recent decade with mounting global issues of the coronavirus, economic downturn and climate change, the University sees a growing demand for pressing solutions to respond to these emerging challenges. To address these and other global issues, it is essential to bring to the University a diversity of talents and open up new horizons in high-impact areas. One of the objectives in HKUST Strategic Plan 2021-2028 ( https://strategicplan.hkust.edu.hk/ ) is to be “A University of TALENTS”, extending our global reservoir of minds and abilities by looking beyond conventional academic disciplines and being open to the recruitment and nurturing of more diverse areas of strength among students, faculty and staff. Concurring with this objective, the University will conduct a strategic hiring campaign aimed at advancing the University’s academic strengths in selected cross-disciplinary areas that are strategically important to HKUST’s future development. We are seeking renowned scholars, academics, leaders or potential leaders in the core cross-disciplinary areas of (A) Biomedical Science and Translational Medicine ; (B) Material Science and Future Energy ; (C) AI, Future Computing and Electronics ; (D) Innovation for Business Management and FinTech ; (E) Environmental Science, Sustainability and Green Tech ; and (F) Art Tech and Humanities . Applications are invited for a number of senior substantiation-track faculty positions at the rank of Professor or Associate Professor in the above areas. Joint appointments in more than one academic department in the University are encouraged . Successful candidates should have a PhD degree in related fields and preferably have demonstrated a solid research track record in the above areas. Apart from having an exceptional research record, successful candidates should demonstrate strong potential as excellent teachers and advisors. Good ability in communicating research problems well beyond one’s own research area, especially with organizations and industry partners, is considered a plus. Appointments can start as early as on 1 June 2023. Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include medical/dental benefits, annual leave, and housing benefits where applicable. Details of the six core cross-disciplinary areas (A) to (F) are as follows: (A) Biomedical Science and Translational Medicine Building on the current strength in biological sciences and translational medicine, the University aims to further enhance the research and educational capacity in this important area to address the pressing health issues locally and worldwide. We are seeking motivated scientists who share the same vision and aim to transform medicine using advanced multi-omics diagnosis, AI-driven preventive medicine data analytics, advanced imaging and data integration, precision medicine by gene editing or advanced therapies, or other advanced approaches that provide important insights into disease mechanisms. The candidate will provide leadership in research and teaching in the general area of biomedical sciences with a clear path to translate pre-clinical research into clinical trials and experimental medicine efforts. The candidate will also be expected to develop new research links with internal units and external partners at the interface between medicine and industry. (B) Material Science and Future Energy HKUST is the world leader in material and energy research. We are seeking talents in the areas including but not limited to advanced electronic materials, photonic materials, low-dimensional and quantum materials, modern functional magnetic materials, polymers, ultra-microscopy and materials characterization, energy materials, clean energy storage solutions, waste to energy, advanced batteries, advanced solar cells, building energy, ocean energy, smart grid, artificial intelligence in power sector, and electric vehicles. (C) AI, Future Computing and Electronics Building on the existing strength in AI, Future Computing and Electronics, we aim to attract outstanding senior scholars to conduct cutting-edge research within the state-of-the-art facilities and demonstrate leadership in research and education excellence endeavors. Areas of interest include but not limited to data science, artificial intelligence, machine learning, future computing, emergent electronics and optoelectronics, computer architecture, integrated circuits, quantum engineering and computing, wireless communications and networking, cybersecurity, human-computer interactions, robotics, IoT, etc. (D) Innovation for Business Management and FinTech We seek talents in cutting-edge research in fintech, sustainability and green finance, business analytics and experimentation, family business, as well as basic business and economics disciplines. A PhD degree in business, economics, computer science or related areas is expected. Areas of interest include but not limited to Blockchain, Robo-advising, Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning in Finance and Business; Business Analytics and Experimental Research; Technological Innovations in Business; the Interplay between Technology, Regulation, and Business; Digital Economy and Financial Inclusion; Family Business and Wealth Management; Sustainability and Green Finance, etc. (E) Environmental Science, Sustainability and Green Tech Building on the existing strength in environmental science and engineering, and sustainability, the University aims to enhance and expand the research and educational capacity to address the pressing environmental issues locally and globally. We are seeking motivated candidates who will provide leadership in research and education in the following broad areas of interest, including but not limited to Air Quality Management; Carbon Reduction Technology, Energy Saving and Green Buildings; Smart City; Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG); Climate Risk Assessment, Modelling and Extreme Weather Prediction; Green Architecture, Green Finance; Life Cycle Assessment; Green Transport; Waste Reduction; Net-zero Electricity Generation, etc. (F) Art Tech and Humanities The Art Tech focus area looks for candidates working on art creation and visual communication with cutting-edge technologies. Candidates working on broad topics on Generative AI for Art or specifically on topics like AR/VR Art with Metaverse, Robotics Art, Data Art, Computer Graphics and 3D animation, AI-generated performance/visual arts, and other forms of computational arts are welcome to apply. In the Humanities, we encourage applications from senior scholars in areas including but not limited to Digital Humanities, Chinese and Comparative Philosophy, Ancient Chinese History, and Cantonese Linguistics. Researchers focusing on health and society, governance, and computational and experimental approaches to social science topics are also encouraged to apply. Application Procedure Please submit the application via the HKUST/HKUST(GZ) Recruitment System ( https://facrecruit.hkust.edu.hk/ ). You should first sign up to create your personal account. At the section of “Application Information”, please select your choice(s) of areas from the “Strategic Hiring” under the “HKUST Hong Kong Campus”. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=8060&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Sustainable Energy and Environment",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Positions in Sustainable Energy and Environment Job Title: 8060 Job ID: Department: Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details In support of the University’s commitment to become a global leader in sustainability education and research, the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering seeks to fill several faculty positions covering the broad areas of sustainable energy and environment. Research fields of interest include, but are not limited to: environment-friendly, energy-efficient and resilient civil systems; sustainable energy infrastructure; renewable energy storage and harvesting systems; sustainable treatment technology for water/wastewater/solid; sustainable environmental technology (bio, nano, valorization, etc.); and sustainable environment assessment and management. We invite applications for substantiation-track faculty positions at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank. Appointment at the Professor rank may also be considered for candidates with outstanding academic credentials and international recognition. Applicants must have a PhD degree in civil or environmental engineering or a related discipline, preferably holding a bachelor’s degree in civil engineering or environmental engineering. The appointees are expected to demonstrate strong potential for effective teaching and promising research, and to complement the Department’s existing strengths in advanced experimental, numerical and information technologies for the development of sustainable energy and environment. For more information about the Department, please visit https://www.ce.ust.hk . The University is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty, and has a range of family-friendly policies in place. Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including medical and dental benefits; annual leave and housing benefits will be provided where applicable. Initial appointment at Assistant/Associate Professor rank will normally be made on a 3-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Appointment at Professor rank will be on substantive basis. Application Procedure Interested candidates are invited to send (i) a curriculum vitae, (ii) a statement of research and teaching interests, and (iii) names and contact information of at least three referees to the Search and Appointments Committee by email to cejob@ust.hk . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Enquiries can also be sent to cejob@ust.hk . (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes only.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=6770&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Faculty Positions Job Title: 6770 Job ID: Department: Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas (EMIA) is a new academic unit established under the Interdisciplinary Programs Office on 1 July 2021. EMIA envisions to foster the agile development of new education programs; contribute to identifying emerging cutting edge and niche topics, such as Artificial Intelligence, Digital Media and Creative Arts; and coordinate interdisciplinary education and research initiatives within and outside HKUST for agile development of emerging areas. The new Division will serve as a cross-disciplinary platform facilitating scholars from different departments, campuses, and universities to incubate and drive research agenda for new and emerging interdisciplinary areas. We are seeking applicants for faculty positions at all ranks who have proven experience in research and teaching of any interdisciplinary areas. Successful applicants will be expected to participate in or lead collaborative teams and research on emerging interdisciplinary topics, nurture undergraduate and postgraduate students with an interdisciplinary approach, and drive various interdisciplinary initiatives of the Division. Applicants should have a PhD degree by the time of employment. The candidates should have proven teaching and advising experience at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels, a strong research and publication record consistent with the candidate’s academic rank, evidence of securing research funding, and a demonstrated ability to work in interdisciplinary teams. Depending on the candidate’s areas of expertise, a joint appointment between the Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas and a relevant academic Department/Division may be possible. More information about the Division is available at https://emia.hkust.edu.hk/ . Applicants with questions may write to ttfhsearch@ust.hk . Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include medical/dental benefits and annual leave. Housing will also be provided where applicable. Application Procedure Application including (i) full curriculum vitae; (ii) separate statements of research interests and teaching philosophy; (iii) a letter of interest summarizing your qualifications, areas of expertise and career goals; (iv) contact information of three qualified referees and (v) five representative research papers (optional), should be submitted via the HKUST Recruitment System ( https://facrecruit.hkust.edu.hk/ ). Applicants should first sign up to create a personal account. In the “Application Information” section, please select “Division of Emerging Interdisciplinary Areas” on “HKUST Hong Kong Campus” for submission of application. Applications are accepted at any time and considered on a rolling basis. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes only.) HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://hrmsxprod.psft.ust.hk:8044/psp/hrmsxprod/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM.HRS_CE.GBL?Page=HRS_CE_JOB_DTL&Action=A&JobOpeningId=6164&SiteId=1000&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Lecturer I",
      "description": "Applicant Home Job Description Senior Lecturer / Lecturer I Job Title: 6164 Job ID: Department: Department of Economics Return to Previous Page Job Posting Details The Department of Economics in the School of Business and Management of The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology seeks applicants for the position of Senior Lecturer / Lecturer I on a part-time or full-time basis. Major responsibilities will be teaching master’s (including MBA) and undergraduate courses, and providing student-related services. Applicants should possess a doctoral degree in economics or a related field and be able to teach in English. They should have a good teaching record and/or extensive professional experience. Those capable of teaching global macroeconomics courses for MBA students are particularly welcome to apply. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment as Lecturer I. (Duration: 1 to 2 years, renewable) Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided. Housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of a 2-year contract. Application Procedure Applicants should send their cover letter and curriculum vitae by e-mail to econjob@ust.hk . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Return to Previous Page t Help test test"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194913": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant (Part-time)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Humanities and Social Science: Division of Humanities Location: Division of Humanities, HKUST, Clear Water Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong SAR The appointee will assist in the preparation of course materials, class administration, facilitating students' in-class discussions, grading, and other teaching related duties as assigned. Applicant should have at least a bachelor's degree in an area of Digital Humanities, Computer Sciences, Data Analysis, Information Systems, or a related field.  They should posses good written and spoken English and Chinese, a general interest in the humanities, along with strong interpersonal skills.  Recent graduates are welcome to apply (Duratioln: 1 year, starting 2 February 2027) Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Fringe benefits including annual leave and medical benefits will be provided. For enquiries, please contact Professor Thorben PELZER at pelzer@ust.hk . In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  To apply, please complete an online application form through the HKUST Careers website ( https:hkustcareers.ust.hk ) and return it online to the Human Resources Office on or before 31 October 2026.  Evidence of technical qualifications, such as in the form of a portfolio, is welcomed.  Applicants will receive an acknowledgement by email upon successful submission.  We thank applicants for their interest but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189734": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Location: Hong Kong Description A Research Fellowship position is now available in the areas of aerodynamics and aeroacoustics at the Aerodynamics Acoustics & Noise Control Technology Centre at the Hong Kong University of Sciences and Technology. The appointee will work on a project that aims to evaluate noise impacts from expanding UAV and eVTOL activities in Hong Kong, which pose risks to urban communities and sensitive ecosystems. It involves extensive testing to develop advanced measurement tools and comprehensive noise databases. The successful candidate will focus on environmental noise impact analysis using advanced sound propagation modelling in complex urban environments. Key Responsibilities Conduct advanced sound propagation modelling for UAV/eVTOL noise in urban settings, accounting for complex terrain, buildings, and atmospheric conditions. Develop and implement high-efficiency numerical algorithms for noise prediction and simulation. Analyze environmental impacts on urban communities and ecological zones, and support the formulation of evidence-based regulatory recommendations. Collaborate with team members on experimental validation, data processing, and reporting for the LAE Regulatory Sandbox project. Publish research findings in high-impact journals and present at relevant conferences. PhD degree in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Acoustics, Applied Mathematics, Physics, or a closely related field. Strong experience in analytical analysis of wave propagation. Proven expertise in the development of high-efficiency algorithms for computational modelling. Solid background in aeroacoustics, sound propagation modelling, or environmental noise assessment is highly preferred. Proficiency in relevant programming languages (e.g., MATLAB, Python, Fortran, C++) and experience with scientific computing. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English; ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative research team. Prior experience with urban environmental modelling or aviation noise research is an advantage. Start Date: 1 September 2026 and onwards Salary: Negotiable based on qualifications and experience. Interested candidates should submit a CV, cover letter to Prof. Xin ZHANG ( aexzhang@ust.hk ). Review begins immediately and continues until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189735": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Location: Hong Kong Description A Research Fellowship position is now available in the areas of aerodynamics and aeroacoustics at the Aerodynamics Acoustics & Noise Control Technology Centre at the Hong Kong University of Sciences and Technology. The appointee will work on a project that aims to evaluate noise impacts from expanding UAV and eVTOL activities in Hong Kong, which pose risks to urban communities and sensitive ecosystems. It involves extensive testing to develop advanced measurement tools and comprehensive noise databases. The successful candidate will focus on experimental measurement of drone noise in controlled and outdoor environments, and on the development of physics-based noise source models for UAV/eVTOL platforms. Key Responsibilities Design and conduct experimental measurements of drone and eVTOL noise in anechoic chamber facilities and outdoor field environments across a range of aircraft types and operating conditions. Develop and validate physics-based noise source models for UAV/eVTOL rotors, capturing aeroacoustic mechanisms such as tonal and broadband noise generation. Process and analyse acoustic measurement data to characterise and quantify UAV/eVTOL noise signatures. Build and maintain a comprehensive noise database to support environmental impact assessments and regulatory recommendations for Hong Kong’s LAE Regulatory Sandbox. Collaborate with modelling and impact assessment team members; publish research findings in high-impact journals and present at relevant conferences. PhD degree in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Acoustics, Applied Mathematics, Physics, or a closely related field. Hands-on experience in acoustic or aeroacoustic experiments, including measurements in anechoic chambers and outdoor/field test environments. Proficiency in acoustic data processing and analysis, including spectral methods, beamforming, and noise source identification techniques. Solid background in aeroacoustics, particularly rotor/propeller noise mechanisms and noise source modelling, is highly preferred. Proficiency in relevant programming languages (e.g., MATLAB, Python, Fortran, C++) and experience with scientific computing. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English; ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative research team. Start Date: 1 September 2026 and onwards Salary: Negotiable based on qualifications and experience. Interested candidates should submit a CV, cover letter to Prof. Xin ZHANG (aexzhang@ust.hk). Review begins immediately and continues until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195369": {
      "title": "Research Associate Laboratory Manager",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Prof Volker Haucke's Lab in Division of Life Science at HKUST, Hong Kong Research in the Haucke laboratory explores the mechanisms of endolysosomal membrane dynamics and nutrient signaling, with a particular focus on their roles in the formation, maintenance and function of the human nervous system in health and disease. Prof. Haucke has received numerous prestigious awards and is an elected member of EMBO, the German National Academy of Sciences Leopoldina and Academia Europaea.  [See: https://leibniz-fmp.de/research/research-section/molecular-physiology-cell-biology/volker-haucke ] The laboratory is relocating from Berlin to HKUST to establish a major new research programme supported by a multi-year Frontier Technology Research Support Scheme (FTRSS) grant. We are seeking an experienced, highly organised and trustworthy Research Associate to serve as Laboratory Manager. This is a pivotal senior role: working closely with the Principal Investigator, the appointee will set up the new laboratory from the ground up, manage its day-to-day operations, budgets and compliance, and act as the PI’s operational deputy for a growing international research group of up to twenty people. The position is full-time and grant-funded, with the research programme funded through 2031/32. An early start (early 2027) is encouraged so that the appointee can lead the laboratory setup. Informal enquiries are welcome. Selected publications: Russo, G., et al., Haucke, V.*, Krauss, M.* (2026) Nanoscale PI(4,5)P2 synthesis by septin-associated PIPKI isoforms controls centralspindlin association with the midbody during cytokinesis. Nat Commun 17, 1482. doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-69224-3 Ebner, M., et al., Haucke, V. (2023) Nutrient-regulated control of lysosome function by signaling lipid conversion. Cell 186, 5328–5346. Bolz, S., et al., Haucke, V. (2023) Synaptotagmin 1-triggered lipid signaling facilitates coupling of exo- and endocytosis. Neuron 111, 3765–3774.e7. Rizalar, F.S., et al., Haucke, V. (2023) Phosphatidylinositol 3,5-bisphosphate facilitates axonal vesicle transport and presynapse assembly. Science 382, 223–230. Jang, W., et al., Haucke, V. (2022) Endosomal lipid signaling reshapes the endoplasmic reticulum to control mitochondrial function. Science 378, eabq5209. Kuijpers, M., et al., Haucke, V. (2021) Neuronal autophagy regulates presynaptic neurotransmission by controlling the axonal endoplasmic reticulum. Neuron 109, 299–313. Lopez-Hernandez, T., et al., Haucke, V. (2020) Endocytic regulation of cellular ion homeostasis controls lysosome biogenesis. Nat. Cell Biol. 22, 815–827. Marat, A.L., et al., Haucke, V. (2017) mTORC1 activity repression by late endosomal phosphatidylinositol 3,4-bisphosphate. Science 356, 968–972. Ketel, K., et al., Haucke, V. (2016) A phosphoinositide conversion mechanism for exit from endosomes. Nature 529, 408–412. von Kleist, L., et al., Haucke, V. (2011) Role of the clathrin terminal domain in regulating coated pit dynamics revealed by small molecule inhibition. Cell 146, 471–484. Duties: Coordinate the set-up and fit-out of the new laboratory: specify and purchase equipment, establish procurement and vendor accounts, and set up stores, inventory and shared systems. Run day-to-day laboratory operations, including ordering of consumables, equipment maintenance and service contracts, and liaison with University core facilities and the Animal and Plant Care Facility (APCF). Manage laboratory and grant budgets (including FTRSS reporting), purchase in line with grant and University rules, track expenditure, and liaise with the Finance Office and the Research and Development Office. Oversee biosafety, chemical and radiation safety, and animal-work protocols and ethics approvals; prepare risk assessments; liaise with the Health, Safety and Environment Office; and maintain records. Onboard new laboratory members (visa and induction support, training, scheduling), coordinate the group and foster a positive, well-organised laboratory culture. Act as the laboratory’s interface with HKUST administration, local vendors and institutional bodies. Depending on background, contribute to or oversee selected experimental methods (e.g. cell and molecular biology, neuronal culture, imaging) and technical training of laboratory members. Perform any other duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator. A PhD in cell biology, molecular biology, neuroscience or a related life-science discipline with relevant post-qualification experience; candidates with a Master’s degree and substantial equivalent experience will also be considered. Substantial experience (typically 5+ years) managing a research laboratory or comparable technical operation in academia or industry. A proven record of independently managing procurement, budgets and regulatory/safety compliance. Excellent organisational, problem-solving and communication skills, with the highest standards of integrity and discretion. The initiative and adaptability to set up a laboratory from scratch and to manage change. Fluency in written and spoken English. Desirable: working proficiency in Cantonese and/or Mandarin; familiarity with Hong Kong research administration, procurement, biosafety and animal-facility procedures; hands-on wet-lab expertise; and experience supporting a mid-to-large international research group or administering competitive grants (e.g. RGC, EU or equivalent). To apply, please click \"Apply Now\" on Interfolio and submit your CV and support documents. Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided. Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194021": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellows/Research Assistants",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Environment and Sustainability Location: Hong Kong The Division of Environment and Sustainability (ENVR) at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) invites applications and expressions of interest for multiple Research Assistant and Postdoctoral Fellow positions, across three major research areas: Air Quality and Health, Climate Adaptation and Resilience, and Sustainable Economy and Integrated Solutions . ENVR brings together expertise across environmental science, engineering, health, data science, economics, finance, policy and the social sciences to address complex environmental and sustainability challenges. We are also expanding our capabilities in software development, artificial intelligence and geospatial technologies to support research, education and the translation of research into practical applications. Air Quality and Health Our research examines the sources, transport, exposure and health impacts of air pollution, integrating atmospheric observations and modelling with exposure assessment, epidemiology and health-risk analysis. A major objective is to translate scientific understanding into practical information that can better protect public health. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in environmental epidemiology, biostatistics, exposure assessment, air-pollution health research and health-risk modelling . Relevant experience may include time-series or cohort analysis, exposure-response relationships, mortality and morbidity analysis, multi-pollutant and compound environmental risks, and integration of environmental, meteorological, demographic and health datasets. Experience with R and/or Python, statistical modelling, GIS, data analytics and machine learning would be advantageous. Climate Adaptation and Resilience Our research addresses the growing risks associated with climate change and extreme weather, spanning high-resolution weather and climate prediction, climate-risk assessment, early-warning systems, and the “last-mile” challenge of translating warnings into effective actions by individuals and communities . We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Weather and climate modelling: high-resolution regional and urban weather/climate modelling; model development and process improvement; extreme precipitation, tropical cyclones, heat and other high-impact weather; MPAS or comparable modelling systems; HPC, model evaluation and diagnostics, and analysis of large climate datasets. Climate risk and early warning: climate-hazard and impact modelling; exposure and vulnerability assessment; impact-based forecasting; development and evaluation of early-warning systems. Last-mile communication and behavioural response: understanding how people perceive, trust, interpret and respond to climate and extreme-weather warnings , and how warnings can be made more personalized, credible and actionable. Relevant expertise may include social and environmental psychology, behavioural science, risk perception, risk communication, decision-making and behavioural intervention design . Community engagement and implementation: working with NGOs, community organizations and vulnerable or high-risk population groups to co-design, test and evaluate warning messages, communication channels and practical interventions, including whether warnings reach the intended populations and lead to appropriate protective actions. Candidates may come from atmospheric science, meteorology, climate science, environmental science, engineering, geography, data science, psychology, behavioural science, public health, social science, risk communication or related disciplines . Interdisciplinary candidates who can connect physical climate-risk information with human behaviour and community implementation are particularly encouraged. Sustainable Economy and Integrated Solutions Our research develops practical and integrated approaches to decarbonization, sustainable development and climate resilience , bringing together science and technology with economic, financial and policy considerations. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Decarbonization and sustainable transport: maritime and other transport sectors, alternative and low-carbon fuels, lifecycle assessment, carbon accounting, and sustainability and certification of fuel pathways. Biodiversity and nature-based solutions: ecosystem and biodiversity modelling, spatial analysis, assessment of ecosystem services, and evaluation of nature-based approaches to climate mitigation and adaptation. Climate risk, economics and finance: quantitative climate-risk assessment, sustainable finance, and the use of insurance and other financial mechanisms to support climate adaptation and resilience . Relevant backgrounds may include environmental science and engineering, energy and transport, economics and finance, operations research, data science, lifecycle assessment, ecology, environmental management and public policy. Cross-cutting Software, AI and GIS Development We are also seeking candidates, particularly at the Research Assistant level , with strong computer science and software-development backgrounds to develop next-generation digital tools supporting environmental research, education and public applications. We are particularly interested in candidates with experience in one or more of the following: Web and mobile application development , including interactive spatial web applications, mapping, geospatial analytics, data collection, visualization and field applications; GIS and geospatial computing , including spatial databases, geoprocessing pipelines, mapping and visualization libraries, and tools such as GDAL/OGR, PostGIS and GeoPandas; AI-assisted software development and applications , including effective use of large language models, generative AI, APIs and AI coding tools to accelerate development and automate research and data workflows; Scientific visualization and communication , including interactive visualization, time-series visualization, animation and AI-assisted generation of explanatory and educational materials; and Development of robust, maintainable scientific software , including appropriate documentation, testing, performance optimization and user-interface design. Candidates should normally have a bachelor’s or master’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related discipline , with sound fundamentals in software engineering, algorithms and data structures. Proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, Python and/or mobile development frameworks such as Flutter, React Native, Swift or Kotlin would be valuable. Experience with web or mobile application development is particularly desirable. Familiarity with geospatial data and environmental applications is advantageous but candidates with a strong computer science background and an interest in applying their skills to environmental and sustainability problems are also encouraged to apply. For Postdoctoral Fellow positions, applicants should have a PhD, or be close to completing a PhD, in a relevant discipline. For Research Assistant positions, applicants should normally have a bachelor’s or master’s degree in a relevant field. Depending on the position or research area, candidates should demonstrate strong quantitative, analytical, computational and/or empirical research capabilities. Good written and oral communication skills and the ability to work independently as well as in interdisciplinary teams are desirable. Candidates are not expected to possess all of the skills listed above . Applicants with strong expertise or research interests in one or more relevant areas are encouraged to apply. Research Assistant and Postdoctoral Fellow positions are available immediately. Review of applications will begin in October 2026, and applications will continue to be accepted and considered until all positions are filled. The level of appointment will be determined according to the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience , in accordance with the University’s prevailing policies and terms of appointment. Interested candidates for Research Assistant and Postdoctoral Fellow positions should submit a curriculum vitae , together with a brief research statement describing their research interests, relevant expertise and experience. Applicants should indicate the research area or technical area that best matches their background and interests. Review of applications for Research Assistant and Postdoctoral Fellow positions will begin in October 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted until all positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194492": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Environment and Sustainability Location: Hong Kong The Division of Environment and Sustainability at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) is opening 1-2 postdoc positions. We are looking for highly motivated scholars with expertise in urban building energy modeling. Scholars with cross-disciplinary experience  (e.g., urban heat modeling, computing methods, and techno-economic analysis) are highly encouraged to apply for this position. The major responsibility of the postdoc is to develop co-simulation methods for building energy modeling and outdoor thermal environment in the content of Hong Kong high-rise built environment. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. For inquiry, please contact Dr. Zhongming LU ( zhongminglu@ust.hk ), Applicants should have a PhD, or be close to completing a PhD, in a relevant discipline."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193808": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong The Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies is looking for a self-motivated and committed Instructional Assistant to support courses of our Dual Degree Program in Technology & Management (T&M-DDP). The appointee will perform a wide spectrum of teaching-related and administrative duties to support the TEMG courses. The appointee is primarily responsible for the following areas: 1. Providing support to TEMG courses (e.g. developing teaching materials and lesson plans, looking for corporate sponsorship, providing class support to teaching faculty and logistics support to course or project-related activities and assessment) 2. Assisting in organizing TEMG1010 co-curricular activities and other student enrichment activities (e,g, mock interview, survival camp, high impact presentation workshop, assessment center simulation, overseas competition, field trip, etc.) 3. Managing IT projects and liaising with external vendors; 4. Performing any other duties as assigned by the supervisors. Working outside normal office hours and outside Hong Kong will be occasionally required. Applicants should have a good bachelor's degree, preferably in Business and Management and Engineering, or a related discipline. The ideal candidate should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, good computing knowledge (e.g., Microsoft Office applications, online course platforms, programming, website development, etc.), and good interpersonal and communication skills. Exposure to consultative problem-solving techniques is a plus. They should enjoy interacting with students; be detail-minded, meticulous and highly organized; and have the ability to meet project milestones and multi-task. (Duration: 2 years, renewable) Please submit the following documents for the application: Curriculum Vitae Teaching statement Past teaching record and evaluation (if applicable) The applicants must first sign up or create a personal account.  Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and candidates are strongly encouraged to submit applications as soon as possible and applications will be considered until the openings are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191940": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow / Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: School of Business and Management(Supporting) Location: School of Business and Management (Institute for Financial Research), The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology  HKUST Business School is searching for a capable and dynamic individual to fill the position of Post-doctoral Fellow / Research Associate in the Institute for Financial Research (IFR). The institute’s mission is to address critical social and economic issues of our time by combining and leveraging knowledge and resources across different intellectual disciplines and fields, as well as from different schools and universities. Our proposed research activities and programs will focus on tackling some of the most important challenges and opportunities in Hong Kong today. The institute has four main research themes: a) Technological Innovations; b) Environmental and Social Responsibility; c) Wealth Management; d) Macro-finance and Geo-economics. The appointee will assist faculty members of the Institute in conducting research in areas related to fintech and/or wealth management and contribute to broader academic and policy discussions under the Institute’s mandate. The job duties include: Conduct research in fintech (blockchain, digital currencies and assets, AI and finance) or wealth management (asset pricing, family office, investment management). Provide editorial and research support for academic publications, policy reports, and grant proposals. Assist in organizing seminars, conferences, and collaborative projects with industry and regulators. Perform data collection, quantitative and qualitative analysis, and database management. Carry out any other duties as assigned by the Institute. Applicants should have a PhD degree in finance, economics, computer science, environmental studies, or related disciplines. They should have genuine interest in research and intellectual curiosity. The ideal candidates should possess an excellent command of verbal and written English and Chinese, and proficiency in programming and statistical software. Relevant research experience is preferred. Interested applicants are requested to send a curriculum vitae with a letter of intent describing their motivation, qualifications, skills and experience relevant to the position, as well as at least one academic paper/writing sample. Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188370": {
      "title": "Teaching Associate / Instructional Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Integrative Systems and Design: Division of Integrative Systems and Design(Supporting) Location: HKUST Clear Water Bay The Division of Integrative Systems and Design (ISD) at HKUST leads a diverse portfolio of undergraduate, postgraduate, and professional programs at the intersection of technology, innovation, and entrepreneurship. ISD is home to the Entrepreneurship Minor (ENTR courses), the BSc in Innovation, Design and Technology (IDT) — Hong Kong's first experiential learning undergraduate programme — as well as the MPhil in Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship (TIE) and the MSc in Technology Leadership and Entrepreneurship (TLE). To support teaching and programme delivery across this portfolio, ISD invites applications for a full-time Teaching Associate (TA) / Instructional Assistant position. Courses and Programmes Supported The appointee will support the delivery of ENTR courses under the ISD Entrepreneurship curriculum, spanning mindset, fundamentals, and skill-set electives that together form the Entrepreneurship Minor pathway. Key Responsibilities Teaching Support ·         Assist course instructors in delivering tutorials, workshops, and experiential learning sessions across ENTR courses ·         Guide and coach student teams through design thinking processes — including problem framing, user research, ideation, prototyping, and iteration ·         Facilitate hands-on sessions on opportunity recognition, startup fundamentals, business model development, and entrepreneurial problem-solving ·         Provide constructive feedback on student assignments, pitches, project submissions, and reflections ·         Assist in developing and updating teaching materials, case studies, and assessment rubrics ·         Handle course coordination tasks including scheduling, student liaison, and attendance Enabling the ENTR Ecosystem ·         Recruit, coordinate, and manage a network of student helpers to support the operational and creative needs of the ENTR programme ·         Oversee student-led production of promotional and educational content, including videos, social media materials, and course promotion assets ·         Nurture and develop student interest groups that organically generate community content — such as podcasts, interview series, opinion pieces, and short-form video — that showcases the ENTR learning experience ·         Foster a vibrant community of active, engaged learners by creating touchpoints and platforms where students can share their entrepreneurial journeys, connect with peers, and inspire one another ·         Support the organisation of programme events such as bootcamps, hackathons, pitch competitions, and community-building activities that extend the learning beyond the classroom Terms and Conditions · Duration: 2 years, renewable · Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience · Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided · A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract Required Qualifications ·         Bachelor’s degree or above in entrepreneurship, business, innovation management, design, or a related field ·         Strong understanding of entrepreneurship principles, startup development, or innovation methodologies, ·         Real world business field experience will be a bonus. ·         Demonstrated ability to apply and facilitate design thinking processes (empathise, define, ideate, prototype, test) in a structured learning environment ·         Experience facilitating group-based, problem-solving activities with diverse student teams ·         Effective communicator and coach who can help students translate ambiguous problems into clear opportunity statements and actionable solutions ·         Ability to manage and motivate student helpers or volunteers, delegating tasks and sustaining engagement across creative and operational workstreams ·         Proactive, collaborative mindset with genuine interest in student development and community building Preferred / Bonus Qualifications · Prior experience teaching, tutoring, or facilitating workshops in entrepreneurship, design thinking, or innovation-related subjects · Startup or venture experience (e.g., founding a company, participating in incubation programmes, pitch competitions, or product commercialization) · Familiarity with human-centred design methodologies, lean startup principles, or business model frameworks (e.g., Business Model Canvas, Value Proposition Design, SAVE, Blue Ocean Strategy) · Experience in content creation, community management, or student engagement programmes — particularly involving video production, podcasting, or social media storytelling · Track record of organising or co-organising student-facing events, activities, or clubs in a university or innovation ecosystem setting · Passion for coaching student innovators and helping teams learn productively from both successes and failures Applicants who combine an entrepreneurial mindset with strong facilitation, community-building, and people management skills, and who are eager to contribute to a dynamic, interdisciplinary learning environment, are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates with less experience may be considered for appointment as an Instructional Assistant. Applications should be sent via Interfolio with a full CV. Review of applications will commence Immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188521": {
      "title": "Research Engineer – Entrepreneurship Programs",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Integrative Systems and Design: Division of Integrative Systems and Design(Supporting) Location: HKUST Clear Water Bay About Division of Integrative Systems and Design The Division aspires to nurture a new generation of innovators who can work across multiple disciplines and create disruptive innovations.  The vision of ISD is to 1) provide state-of-the-art project-based experiential learning in education and 2) be a cradle for nurturing innovators and researchers with a design and system thinking mindset as well as an entrepreneurial spirit.  The Division provides comprehensive teaching and research programs in integrated design and systems thinking.  The academic degrees offered by ISD are a BSc in Innovation, Design and Technology, a MSc in Technology Leadership & Entrepreneurship, a MPhil degree in Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship and a PhD and MPhil programs in Integrative Systems and Design.  We are expanding rapidly and looking to broaden into disciplines such as sports, marine technology and medical technology. We are seeking a Research Engineer to support technology innovation and entrepreneurship initiatives for the TIE (Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship) and TLE (Technology, Leadership and Entrepreneurship) programs. This role focuses on guiding multidisciplinary development projects with strong commercialization potential and facilitating knowledge transfer across teams. Key Responsibilities Manage and oversee TIE, TLE projects from concept to implementation. Guide development and knowledge transfer projects, particularly those with entrepreneurial and commercialization intent. Support interdisciplinary teams working across hardware and software domains. Ensure effective project planning, execution, and delivery across multiple concurrent initiatives. Contribute to a collaborative ecosystem involving students, researchers, and industry partners. Preferred Qualifications PhD degree with at least 2 years’ post-qualification experience in R&D or equivalent; or MPhil/MSc degree with at least 5 years’ post-qualification experience in R&D or equivalent Experience in academic or research environments. Familiarity with experiential learning models. Knowledge of ergonomics and CMF (color, material, finish/feel) considerations in product design. Requirements Broad product management experience across the full lifecycle of consumer product design and development. Technical exposure to embedded systems, mechanical and mechatronics design, robotics and control systems, and software development. Strong project and time management skills, with the ability to handle multiple diverse projects simultaneously. Demonstrated ability to work in structured, deadline-driven environments. Applications should be sent via Interfolio with a full CV. Review of applications will commence Immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188522": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Engineer – Entrepreneurship Programs",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Integrative Systems and Design: Division of Integrative Systems and Design(Supporting) Location: HKUST Clear Water Bay About Division of Integrative Systems and Design The Division aspires to nurture a new generation of innovators who can work across multiple disciplines and create disruptive innovations.  The vision of ISD is to 1) provide state-of-the-art project-based experiential learning in education and 2) be a cradle for nurturing innovators and researchers with a design and system thinking mindset as well as an entrepreneurial spirit.  The Division provides comprehensive teaching and research programs in integrated design and systems thinking.  The academic degrees offered by ISD are a BSc in Innovation, Design and Technology, a MSc in Technology Leadership & Entrepreneurship, a MPhil degree in Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship and a PhD and MPhil programs in Integrative Systems and Design.  We are expanding rapidly and looking to broaden into disciplines such as sports, marine technology and medical technology. We are seeking an Assistant Research Engineer to support student-focused innovation and entrepreneurship initiatives within the TLE (Technology Learning and Entrepreneurship) and MEng in Design Innovation programs. This role emphasizes hands-on engagement with student teams and the development of training ecosystems for entrepreneurial learning. Key Responsibilities Manage TLE projects and coordinate student project teams. Organize and deliver developmental and training activities for entrepreneurial students across TLE and TIE programs. Liaise with external incubators and accelerators to support student ventures. Mentor student teams in the design and development of MVPs and functional prototypes. Contribute to the development of structured learning materials for experiential education. Preferred Qualifications MPhil/MSc degree; or Bachelor’s degree with at least 1 year’s post-qualification experience in R&D or equivalent Experience working with student-led innovation or startup programs. Familiarity with incubation, acceleration, or venture-building environments. Strong communication and mentoring skills. Requirements Broad experience in entrepreneurship, innovation, or startup ecosystems. Strong technical background in robotics, artificial intelligence, and embedded systems. Proven ability to guide student teams in product development and prototyping. Ability to design and deliver training materials in an experiential learning context. Applications should be sent via Interfolio with a full CV. Review of applications will commence Immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191939": {
      "title": "Teaching Associate / Instructional Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Integrative Systems and Design: Division of Integrative Systems and Design(Supporting) Location: HKUST Clear Water Bay The Division of Integrative Systems and Design runs a wide variety of teaching and research projects that are multi-disciplinary. These projects use a wide range of technology and tools, including mechanical design and machines, electronic systems design, materials and shape design and IT systems design. The Division is looking for a candidate who is interested in computer-aided design and manufacturing, artificial intelligence, or product design. The appointee is expected to (a) assist course instructors in running innovation project courses; (b) conduct course tutorials/workshops; and (c) organize and facilitate events/activities. Applicants should possess strong skills in one or more of the following areas: CAD/CAM tools and generative design, digital fabrication and rapid prototyping, computer vision, machine learning and artificial intelligence, deep learning, foundation models, multimodal AI systems, human-centered design, or computational design. The ideal candidate should have good communication skills and be passionate about working with motivated and dynamic students. Candidates with less work experience may be considered for appointment as an Instructional Assistant Applications should be sent via Interfolio with a full CV. Review of applications will commence Immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188999": {
      "title": "Instructor Assistant/Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Accounting: Department of Accounting(Supporting) Location: Dept of Accounting, 6/F, Lee Shau Kee Business Bldg., Clearwater Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong. The appointee will assist in grading and providing other teaching support to courses in the Master of Science in Accounting Program. Applicants should have a good bachelor’s degree in accounting with at least 1 to 3 years of relevant experience, preferably in auditing and/or taxation. Applicants with law background is preferred. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills; a good command of both written and spoken English; and good computer skills are required. He/She should be mature, attentive to details and be able to work independently.  Proficiency in Mandarin is preferred. Applicants with more years of relevant experience or a master’s degree may be considered for appointment as Teaching Associate (Duration: 1 or 2 years, renewable) In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  Interested candidates should complete the online application via Interfolio by clicking the “Apply Now” button on this page. A full CV must be included with the application. Review of applications will commence from Thursday, 10 July 2026 and will continue until the positions are filled. Applicants will receive an acknowledgement by email upon successful submission.  We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191040": {
      "title": "Full-time Research Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Accounting: Department of Accounting(Supporting) Location: Dept of Accounting, Rm 6018, 6/F, Lee Shau Kee Business Bldg, Clearwater Bay, Kowloon, Hong Kong. The appointee will assist Professor Yue Zheng in the Department of Accounting at HKUST in her academic research activities.  Key responsibilites inlcude data collection, data cleaning, data analysis, and any other duties as assigned. Duration of appointment:  6 months (renewable) 1. A bachelor's or master's degree in Business, Computer Science, Information Systems or other relevant areas; 2. Experience in web crawling and text analysis using Python, machine learning, and LLM; 3. Good command of written and spoken English; 4. Hard-working, timely communication, and responsible. Screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Compensation: Full-time position, salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191563": {
      "title": "Full-time Research Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Finance: Department of Finance(Supporting) Location: Clear Water Bay, Hong Kong The HKUST Institute for Financial Research - Macro-Finance Research Center is recruiting Research Assistants for a research team working on quantitative macro-finance. The role is an ideal stepping stone to a top PhD program and emphasizes numerical and machine-learning methods for solving macroeconomic and financial models. Duration of appointment: 1-2 years (renewable) Responsibilities The successful candidate will: •       Implement and solve dynamic macro and asset pricing models using numerical and machine-learning techniques. •       Build, clean, and analyze large financial and macroeconomic datasets. •       Support active research projects and the Center's data infrastructure and reports. Applicants should possess: •       Bachelor's or master's degree (completed or expected before start) in Economics, Finance, Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or a related quantitative field. •       Strong programming and numerical skills, ideally including machine-learning methods (Python, Julia, MATLAB, or similar). •       Solid foundation in econometrics and quantitative methods; strong attention to detail. •       Intention to pursue a PhD in finance or economics is a plus. The starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience, and fringe benefits, including annual leave and medical benefits, when applicable, will be provided. Mentorship and support for PhD applications provided. Application Procedure In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  Interested candidates should complete the online application via Interfolio by clicking the “Apply Now” button on this page and submit a cover letter, CV, and transcript(s) (as a single PDF). Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the outcome."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191564": {
      "title": "Full-time Post-Doctoral Fellow / Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Finance: Department of Finance(Supporting) Location: Clear Water Bay, Hong Kong The HKUST Institute for Financial Research - Macro-Finance Research Center seeks one or more Post-Doctoral Fellows / Research Associates to join a research team working on quantitative macro-finance, with a strong emphasis on computational and machine-learning methods for solving and estimating macroeconomic and financial models. Duration of appointment: 1-2 years (renewable) Responsibilities The successful candidate will: •       Develop and solve high-dimensional dynamic macroeconomic and asset pricing models using modern numerical and machine-learning techniques. •       Estimate structural and empirical models on large financial and macroeconomic datasets. •       Contribute to the Center's broader research activities, including drafting its annual report on the Chinese economy, building and maintaining the Center's data infrastructure, and supporting its other flagship publications. •       Help mentor junior research staff. Applicants should possess: •       PhD (completed or expected before start) in Finance, Economics, or a related quantitative field. •       Strong numerical and computational skills, including machine-learning and deep-learning methods for solving dynamic models (e.g., neural-network solution methods, reinforcement learning, high-dimensional approximation). •       Advanced programming (Python, Julia, MATLAB, or similar) and experience with large datasets. •       Demonstrated capacity for independent, publishable research. The starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience, and fringe benefits, including annual leave and medical benefits, when applicable, will be provided. Application Procedure In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  Interested candidates should complete the online application via Interfolio by clicking the “Apply Now” button on this page and submit a cover letter, CV, and job-market paper or writing sample (as a single PDF) . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the outcome."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193164": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management(Supporting): Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management - OM group Location: Hong Kong The Principal Investigator (PI) is seeking a Research Assistant to support several projects in operations management. The successful candidate will conduct literature reviews, clean and analyze data, and assist with the preparation of academic papers and research grant applications. The position may also involve other research-related and ad hoc tasks assigned by the PI. Applicants should hold a bachelor’s or master’s degree in statistics, economics, finance, operations management, or a related field. HKUST graduates are welcome to apply. Preference will be given to candidates with relevant research experience and programming skills in Python, R, and/or Stata. Applicants should also have strong written and spoken English skills and be able to work independently. Applicants should submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae (CV). All materials should be submitted via interfolio by 31 December, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185567": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Management: Department of Management(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong The Department of Management is seeking high-calibre candidates to fill the position of Instructional Assistant. The appointee will provide support in the preparation of course materials, class administration, grading of assignments, and invigilation of examinations. The position requires flexibility to work outside normal office hours when necessary, such as during examination periods and immediately thereafter. Applicants should hold a bachelor’s degree, preferably with a major in business, management, psychology, or a related social science discipline. They should possess strong written and spoken English and Chinese, good analytical and computing skills, and effective interpersonal abilities. The successful candidate should be a reliable team player. Fresh graduates are welcome to apply. (Duration: 2 years, renewable) Interested candidates are invited to submit the required materials electronically via Interfolio ( https://apply.interfolio.com/185567 ). Required materials include: Cover letter CV Online application forms Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186076": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Management: Department of Management(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong The appointee will support a faculty member in the Department of Management in conducting behavioral research, including the design, administration, and analysis of experimental and survey-based studies. The role involves close collaboration with the Principal Investigator on multiple ongoing projects. Major duties of the appointee may include: Programming, testing, and deploying surveys and experiments using Qualtrics Learning specific software use Recruiting and managing study participants through Prolific and other platforms Administering studies and assisting with in-person or online data collection, including manual data collection where required Reviewing and refining study materials, stimuli, and protocols prior to launch Collecting, cleaning, and organizing archival data Conducting literature reviews Supporting general research operations and undertaking other duties as assigned Applicants should have a bachelor's degree or above in management, psychology, economics, behavioral science, or a related discipline, and an excellent command of written and spoken English. The ideal candidate should have a sincere interest in academic research, strong attention to detail, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Prior experience with Qualtrics, Prolific, and R / R Studio is an advantage. (Duration: 3 months, with the possibility of extension up to 4 months; full-time or part-time arrangements considered) Interested candidates are invited to submit the required materials electronically via Interfolio ( https://apply.interfolio.com/186076 ). Required materials include: Cover letter CV Online application forms Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Fringe benefits including medical benefits and paid leave will be provided where applicable. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the position is filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194571": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Part-time)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Humanities and Social Science: Division of Humanities: Division of Humanities(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong The Division of Humanities is looking for a high calibre candidate to fill the position of part-time Research Assistant to support Data Analysis & Project Management in Digital Humanities & AI. Major duties of the appointee include: Research: Data procurement, cleaning, analysis, documentation, archiving. Coordination: Managing preparations for academic events. Outreach: Leading preparations for an online exhibition and public presentations. Applications will only be considered from candidates who meet all the stated essential criteria listed below: Applicants should possess at least a bachelor’s degree or equivalent with knowledge of the written Chinese language . The ideal candidate should possess strong expertise in data analysis using R or Python, alongside a general interest in history and China studies . Experience with GIS, GeoAI, and neural networks, as well as fluency in English and/or one or more of Hong Kong’s community languages would be an advantage. Proven ability to write well in academic English will be considered a strong advantage. (Duration: 1 year) Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits including paid leave and medical benefits may be provided. In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  To apply, please submit (i) the online application form and (ii) 1-page CV and a portfolio (maximum of 3 pages; links to Git repositories or projects are welcome) through the HKUST Careers website ( https://hkustcareers.ust.hk ). Your cover letter should clearly demonstrate how you meet the essential criteria and, where applicable, the preferred characteristics outlined in the advertisement, supported by explicit examples. Applications must be submitted online to the Human Resources Office on or before Saturday 31st October 2026 . Applicants will receive an acknowledgement by email upon successful submission. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.) Human Resources Office"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194668": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Part-time)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Humanities and Social Science: Division of Humanities: Division of Humanities(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong The Division of Humanities is looking for a high-calibre candidate to fill the position of part-time Research Assistant to support research in Digital Humanities & AI. Major duties of the appointee include: Research : Data analysis, cleaning, documentation, and archiving. Development : Co-design of AI-assisted digital humanities workflows and interfaces. Server administration : Maintenance of virtual server & HPC/Slurm interaction with clusters. Only applications that meet all the essential criteria below will be considered: Applicants should possess at least a bachelor’s degree or equivalent with knowledge of the written Chinese language . The ideal candidate should possess strong expertise in coding and neural networks, coupled with a general interest in the humanities and China studies . Experience with databases, data analysis, dedicated server dashboards, and HPC/Slurm environments, as well as fluency in English and/or one or more of Hong Kong’s community languages would be an advantage. Proven ability to write well in academic English will be considered a strong advantage. (Duration: 1 year) Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Fringe benefits including paid leave and medical benefit may be provided. In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  To apply, please submit (i) the online application form and (ii) 1-page CV and a portfolio (maximum of 3 pages; links to Git repositories or projects are welcome) through the HKUST Careers website ( https://hkustcareers.ust.hk ). Your cover letter should clearly demonstrate how you meet the essential criteria and, where applicable, the preferred characteristics outlined in the advertisement, supported by explicit examples. Applications must be submitted online to the Human Resources Office on or before 31 st October 2026 .  Applicants will receive an acknowledgement by email upon successful submission.  We thank applicants for their interest but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192140": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Full-time)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering: Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong Prof. Hong K. LO is leading a research project titled “Improving Fleet & Driver Shift Operating Efficiency via a Next Generation Taxi Operating System”, funded by Smart Traffic Fund. The project aims to develop a taxi operating system for enhancing overall taxi operational efficiency by utilizing newly developed taxi meters to collect real-time vehicle information and trip data. The project team will develop an AI-assisted Insights Map to provide taxi drivers with information on potentially profitable trip locations. We are currently seeking motivated individuals to join our team as Research Associate. Duration of appointment: 1 year to 2 years (renewable) Key Responsibilities • Proactively identify, acquire, and assess relevant datasets for project needs, performing data fusion processes and conducting in-depth statistical analyses to uncover patterns and insights. • Manage and maintain the large-scale taxi trajectories and relevant databases, ensuring data quality and accessibility for the research team. • Oversee the management of GPU/CPU server clusters for AI model training. • Develop and train machine learning models for real-time taxi drivers’ profitability prediction. • Design intuitive frontend interfaces for drivers to interact with the model in real-world scenarios. • Support and perform other relevant duties as required. • Doctoral degree in Transportation Engineering, Computer Science, Information Technology or related fields. • Proficiency in machine learning, artificial intelligence and data analytics, and in research project management; R&D experience in the industry is a plus. • Solid experience in the configuration of GPU/CPU clusters and management of high-speed storage dedicated to the clusters. • Strong knowledge of Python frameworks and databases (SQL); familiarity with additional programming languages such as C++ and Java are advantageous. • Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a self-motivated and organized approach to teamwork. If you are passionate about improving operational efficiency of the taxi industry through technology and data analysis, we encourage you to apply and join our dedicated research team. Competitive starting salary based on qualifications and experience. To apply, please click \"Apply Now\" on Interfolio and submit your CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190658": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Backend Development)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Computer Science and Engineering: Department of Computer Science and Engineering(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong The Department of Computer Science and Engineering is seeking a motivated Research Assistant (Backend Development) to join the UpCareer Project , an innovative AI-driven gamification platform designed to support neurodiverse career development. The platform combines interactive simulations, artificial intelligence, and data analytics to help individuals discover, develop, and succeed in meaningful career pathways. This position offers an exciting opportunity to gain hands-on experience building a real-world AI product while collaborating with leading researchers, software developers, and industry partners. About the Role As a Backend Developer within the project team, you will contribute to the design, development, and maintenance of backend systems, APIs, and data infrastructure that power the UpCareer platform. You'll work alongside our front-end developer, AI research team at HKUST, and external technology partners to deliver scalable and impactful solutions. What You'll Be Working On You will collaborate closely with: The HKUST AI Research Team , who develop the AI recommendation models integrated into the platform. Redmer Productions , the team behind the BLADE gamification platform, analytics dashboard, and reporting systems. Front-End Developers , ensuring seamless integration between client applications and backend services. Key Responsibilities Develop and maintain backend features supporting the UpCareer platform, dashboards, and reporting services. Build and enhance backend functionality within the BLADE gamification platform, including gameplay data capture and scoring mechanisms. Design and implement APIs for integrating AI recommendation models into the platform. Develop and maintain data schemas covering demographic, behavioural, attitudinal, and in-game performance data. Support data cleaning, mining, and analytics activities to facilitate AI model development and research. Collaborate with front-end developers to define API specifications and resolve integration issues. Conduct testing, debugging, and technical documentation of backend systems. Support ongoing maintenance and enhancement of platform infrastructure following deployment. What We're Looking For Essential Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related discipline (final-year students will also be considered). Experience with backend technologies such as: Node.js Express.js TypeScript MongoDB / Mongoose Understanding of database design principles, including relational and/or NoSQL databases. Familiarity with Git and collaborative software development practices. Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese. Strong problem-solving ability and enthusiasm for learning new technologies. Desirable Skills Experience with Python and API development frameworks such as Flask. Interest or experience in data analytics, including SQL, Pandas, or NumPy. Exposure to cloud technologies, managed databases, or Kubernetes environments. Experience gained through internships, academic projects, personal projects, or research activities. Duration: 1 to 2 years (renewable) Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and expeirence.  Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided.  Where applicable, a gratuity will be payable upon successful comletion of the 2-year contract. In support of a green work environment, we accept applications submitted online only.  Interested candidates should complete the online application via Interfolio by clicking the “Apply Now” button on this page. A full CV must be included with the application. Review of applications will commence from 14 August 2026 and will continue until the position is filled.  Interested candidates are encouraged to apply as early as possible.  Applicants will receive an acknowledgement by email upon successful submission.  We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the result of the application."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192027": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow (AI-Driven Peptide Drug Design and Modeling)",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Department of Computer Science and Engineering: Department of Computer Science and Engineering(Supporting) Location: Hong Kong The Department of Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Fellow to join an international team of experts in AI, peptide drug design, mRNA display, and immunology . Supported by industry, the appointee will lead the development and application of advanced computational methodologies — integrating artificial intelligence, molecular dynamics simulations, and molecular docking — to accelerate cyclic peptide drug discovery. The appointee's work will focus on algorithm design for modeling and designing novel therapeutics. Key Responsibilities Establish predictive models for both natural and non-natural amino acid cyclic peptides. Optimize targets for receptor complex and membrane transport. Characterize essential parameters governing membrane permeability for peptide delivery. Lead the development and application of advanced computational methodologies integrating AI, molecular dynamics simulations, and molecular docking. Essential Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or a closely related field. Demonstrated experience in training or fine-tuning foundation models for structural biology. Strong background in bioinformatics data curation, processing, and cleaning. Solid track record of relevant academic publications. Duration: Initial 1-year contract with the possibility of renewal and long-term employment based on performance and mutual agreement. Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and expeirence.  Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided. Applications are accepted on a rolling basis and will be reviewed immediately upon receipt until the position is filled. Interested candidates should complete the online application via Interfolio by clicking the “Apply Now” button on this page. A CV/ resume, a brief cover letter outlining relevant computational/AI experience, and a list of publications should be included in the application."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192893": {
      "title": "Teaching Associate / Instructional Assistant",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Engineering: Center for Engineering Education Innovation Location: HKUST Clear Water Bay The Center for Engineering Education Innovation (E2I), operating under the School of Engineering, is dedicated to enriching the learning and teaching experience for both students and faculty members. The Center supports student and faculty development by promoting innovative teaching and learning approaches and advancing experiential, hands-on, and technology-enabled learning across the School of Engineering. The appointee will provide teaching, instructional, and administrative support for engineering courses and contribute to a range of student learning and development initiatives. Responsibilities include: Taking an active role in teaching engineering courses and providing instructional support to course instructors; Assisting in the planning and implementation of student learning and development activities, including seminars, academic talks, workshops, company visits, competitions, and other experiential learning programs; Supporting students in project-based and hands-on learning activities, including engineering projects, prototyping, and other experiential learning initiatives; Supporting the operation and development of teaching laboratories, makerspaces, and other experiential learning facilities, including the preparation and coordination of equipment, learning resources, and student activities; Contributing to the development and implementation of innovative teaching and learning initiatives, including those involving emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence, robotics, and digital fabrication; and Performing other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Center Director. Applicants should hold a bachelor’s, master’s, or doctoral degree in engineering or a related discipline from a recognized university. Candidates with different levels of academic qualifications and relevant professional experience are welcome to apply. Prior experience in engineering education, teaching and learning support, student development, laboratory or makerspace operation, experiential learning, artificial intelligence, robotics, digital fabrication, or related areas is not required but would be an advantage. The ideal candidate should be able to work both independently and collaboratively in a cross-functional environment, demonstrate a strong sense of responsibility, and maintain a service-oriented mindset. A genuine interest in working with students and supporting their learning and development is essential. Good written and spoken English communication skills are expected, while proficiency in Chinese is desirable. Depending on qualifications and relevant experience, applicants may be considered for appointment as Teaching Associate or Instructional Assistant . (Duration: 2 years, renewable) Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits, including annual leave, medical, and dental benefits, will be provided in accordance with the University’s policy. To apply, click “Apply Now” on this page and submit your application together with a full CV via Interfolio. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194909": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Finance Location: Hong Kong The School of Business and Management of the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST Business School) invites applications for full-time tenured (associate or full professor level) or tenure-track (assistant level) faculty in the Department of Finance effective July 2027, or as soon thereafter as possible, to conduct applied research and related teaching. THE UNIVERSITY is a publicly-funded research-intensive university with a founding mandate to help spur economic development in Hong Kong and the region. HKUST BUSINESS SCHOOL has risen to international prominence in a remarkably short time, achieving widespread global recognition and a variety of prestigious academic rankings. Always striving for excellence, our strength lies in our full range of program offerings, our high-quality research, conducted by our world-class faculty, and our diverse and high-caliber students. THE DEPARTMENT OF FINANCE endeavors to deliver quality teaching and world-class research.  Our finance research aims to achieve both academic excellence and practical relevance. For more information about HKUST, please visit http://www.ust.hk/about-hkust/ . Applicants must have a Ph.D. in a related field by the start of the employment and should be capable of teaching courses at the undergraduate, MBA, and Ph.D. levels. Applicants are invited to send your curriculum vitae, recent publications, research papers, and three letters of recommendation electronically by the end of Nov 13, 2026.  The selection continues until suitable appointments are made. Priority will be given to applications that are received by Nov 13, 2026. Applications after that date will be considered on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196417": {
      "title": "CHEM - Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Department of Chemistry Location: Hong Kong Posted: Oct 27, 2026 The Department of Chemistry at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology invites applications for the role of faculty in all areas of chemistry and at all ranks. About the role Successful candidates are expected to develop strong, independent and innovative programs of externally sponsored research; teach effectively in <...> at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and participate in services of the Department, the School and the University. The Department of Chemistry The Department of Chemistry is comprised of around 25 faculty members and is on track for further expansion. Research interests and expertise  of  faculty members include  areas  across Analytical/Environmental Chemistry,  Synthetic Organic and  Inorganic Chemistry,  Materials Chemistry,  Physical and  Computational Chemistry, Biochemistry and  Medicinal Chemistry.  The  Department’s  undergraduate program aims  to provide students with a solid foundation for analytical thinking and problem solving to prepare students for further  studies and  career development in  fields  related to  chemical science  and  technology.  Our postgraduate  programs place additional emphasis on  training in  original research and  is focused on fundamental, interdisciplinary, and applied research topics. The School of Science The School of Science is the home to five world-class departments, including Chemistry, Life Science, Mathematics, Ocean  Science  and  Physics. Current enrollment at  the  school  includes over 2,000 undergraduate students and around 1,000  postgraduate students. The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology HKUST is a world-class university ranked top in Asia and globally, recognized for research excellence and interdisciplinary innovation. Join a vibrant faculty shaping the future of education, research, and entrepreneurship. Learn more at https://hkust.edu.hk . ​Applicants should have: A <Education level, e.g. PhD / Dr / MD > degree in <subject> or or a closely related field <Period , e.g. 1 - 3 years of > post-qualification experience in <FIELD specific> Deep expertise on <FIELD Specific> A proven track record of research excellence and a steadfast commitment to high-quality teaching and mentorship Proven ability to work effectively in multidisciplinary, collaborative environments A strong record of independent research, successful grant applications (funding), and academic leadership ... Salary is highly competitive and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include annual leave, medical and dental benefits. Housing benefits will also be provided where applicable. Appointment at Professor rank will be on substantive basis. Initial appointment at the Assistant Professor/Associate Professor rank will normally be made on a three-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract. Please submit the following documents for application: Curriculum Vitae Research statement Teaching statement Contact Information for three qualified referees ... The applicants must first sign up or create a personal account.  Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and candidates are strongly encouraged to submit applications as soon as possible and applications will be considered until the openings are filled. (Information provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.  Applicants should read the Personal Information Collection Statement before submission of application.)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196059": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow / Research Associate / Visiting Scholar",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Life Science at HKUST, Hong Kong Posted: Oct 27, 2026 The laboratories of Prof. Wei Yang in the Division of Life Science at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seek talented and highly motivated graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and research assistant professors. Our research focuses on genome maintenance with the goal of uncovering fundamental molecular mechanisms and translating mechanistic insights into targeted therapeutics. We integrate cutting-edge approaches in genomics, mass spectrometry, machine learning, and structural biology. Our research spans genome maintenance and cellular signal transduction, with the goal of uncovering fundamental molecular mechanisms and translating mechanistic insights into targeted therapeutics. We integrate cutting-edge approaches in genomics, mass spectrometry, artificial intelligence, and structural biology. Our laboratories are located on HKUST’s beautiful Clear Water Bay campus in Kowloon, Hong Kong. Housing is available on campus or within easy commuting distance. Applicants should hold a PhD, MPhil, or MSc degree in Biochemistry, Pharmacology, Biology, or a related discipline. Candidates should have 1 to 3 years of relevant research experience, together with a strong background in biochemistry, molecular biology, and cell biology. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Multiple positions are available. Candidates interested in genome maintenance should apply through the Interfolio online application system by pressing APPLY button and submit a curriculum vitae, a summary of research experience and interests, and the names and contact information of two referees. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the positions will remain open until filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196271": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow / Research Associate / Visiting Scholar",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Life Science at HKUST, Hong Kong Posted: Oct 27, 2026 The laboratories of Prof. Daniel Leahy in the Division of Life Science at the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST) seek talented and highly motivated graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and research assistant professors. Research in our laboratory involves use of cryo-electron microscopy and tomography to investigate the structure, function, and organization of intact receptor tyrosine kinases in bilayer membranes. Our research spans genome maintenance and cellular signal transduction, with the goal of uncovering fundamental molecular mechanisms and translating mechanistic insights into targeted therapeutics. We integrate cutting-edge approaches in genomics, mass spectrometry, artificial intelligence, and structural biology. Our laboratories are located on HKUST’s beautiful Clear Water Bay campus in Kowloon, Hong Kong. Housing is available on campus or within easy commuting distance. Applicants should hold a PhD, MPhil, or MSc degree in Biochemistry, Pharmacology, Biology, or a related discipline. Candidates should have 1 to 3 years of relevant research experience, together with a strong background in biochemistry, molecular biology, and cell biology. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Multiple positions are available. Candidates interested in signal transduction and receptor tyrosine kinases should apply through the Interfolio online application system by clicking APPLY button and submit a curriculum vitae, a summary of research experience and interests, and the names and contact information of two referees. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the positions will remain open until filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196508": {
      "title": "Principal Research Scientist",
      "description": "Department: Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Science: Division of Life Science Location: Prof Volker Haucke's Lab in Division of Life Science at HKUST, Hong Kong Posted: Oct 28, 2026 Deadline: Nov 05, 2026 Job description – key duties and responsibilities •Establish and lead a state-of-the-art deep proteomics and interactomics capability at HKUST, centred on proteome-wide crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS). •Define the mass spectrometry instrumentation, sample-preparation infrastructure and computing resources needed, and oversee their purchase, installation and commissioning. •Develop, optimise and set up on site workflows for quantitative proteomics, crosslinking MS, spatial proteomics and protein–protein interaction mapping in cells, organelles and tissues, including the data-analysis pipelines that go with them. •Develop new methods in proteomics and XL-MS (crosslinker chemistry, enrichment strategies, acquisition methods, computational and AI-based search and validation tools) and publish them in leading international journals. •Plan and run collaborative research projects with faculty in the Division of Life Science and across HKUST. Application areas include membrane trafficking, autophagy, neurobiology, and stem cell quiescence and ageing. •Combine XL-MS data with structural modelling (e.g. AlphaFold-based approaches) and with imaging and cryo-EM data to produce models of protein complexes and cellular organisation. •Train and supervise research staff, postdoctoral fellows and research students in proteomics and XL-MS methods. Make the technology available to the wider HKUST research community. •Help secure external research funding and build international collaborations. •Oversee quality control, data management and safe operation of the proteomics facilities. Essential •PhD in biochemistry, analytical chemistry, molecular biology or a related field, followed by at least 10 years of postdoctoral and independent research experience. •Internationally recognised expertise in developing crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) methods, covering crosslinker chemistry, sample preparation, MS acquisition and/or computational analysis. •A proven record of methods development in proteomics in general, shown by high-impact publications as first and as senior/corresponding author in leading journals (e.g. Nature Methods, Nature Communications, Angewandte Chemie, or equivalent). •Extensive hands-on experience with high-resolution Orbitrap-class mass spectrometers, nano-LC systems and large-scale proteomic data analysis. •Experience of independently leading a research group and/or managing a mass spectrometry or proteomics core facility, including setting up instruments and workflows. •A record of successful interdisciplinary collaborations that apply proteomics and interactomics to questions in cell biology, structural biology or neuroscience. •Experience training and supervising scientists at different career stages. •Excellent communication skills in English. Desirable •A record of winning competitive research funding (e.g. ERC or equivalent national or international grants). •Experience developing open-source or commercially licensed software for proteomics or XL-MS data analysis. •Experience with spatial proteomics and with combining MS data with structural modelling and cryo-EM. •International recognition through awards and invited lectures at major conferences. To apply, please click \"Apply Now\" on Interfolio and submit your CV and support documents. Starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Fringe benefits including annual leave, medical and dental benefits will be provided. Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled."
    }
  },
